window.EXAM_DATA = {"id":"cca-scenario-a","title":"시나리오 모의고사 A","subtitle":"Scenario Mock A · 60 Questions","kind":"mock","timeLimitSec":7200,"passScaled":720,"domains":{"1":"Agentic Architecture & Orchestration","2":"Tool Design & MCP Integration","3":"Claude Code Configuration & Workflows","4":"Prompt Engineering & Structured Output","5":"Context Management & Reliability"},"domainWeights":{"1":27,"2":18,"3":20,"4":20,"5":15},"domainShort":{"1":"Agentic","2":"Tools & MCP","3":"Claude Code","4":"Prompting","5":"Context"},"note":"자체 제작 CCAR-F 연습 문제입니다(비공식). 문제·보기는 영어, 해설은 한국어. 이 도구의 점수식은 공식 채점과 다릅니다.","questions":[{"domain":1,"stem":"During load testing, about 9% of conversations end with Tidewater Assist saying \"Let me check that order for you\" and then going silent; the customer never receives an answer. Logs show the final API response in those runs contained a short text block followed by a `tool_use` block for `lookup_order`. The loop is written as follows:\n\nwhile True:\n    resp = client.messages.create(model=MODEL, tools=TOOLS, messages=msgs)\n    msgs.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": resp.content})\n    if any(block.type == \"text\" for block in resp.content):\n        send_to_customer(resp.content)\n        break\n    msgs.append(run_tools(resp.content))\n\nWhat is the most effective fix?","options":["Instruct the model in the system prompt never to write any narration text in the same turn in which it decides to request a tool call from the MCP server.","Raise `max_tokens` so the model can finish the whole answer in one response, preventing it from stopping partway through a lookup.","Drive the loop from `stop_reason`: while it is `\"tool_use\"`, run tools and append results; exit only on `\"end_turn\"`, streaming interim text.","Add a maximum iteration count of ten so the loop cannot stall, and send a generic apology message whenever that cap is reached."],"answer":2,"explanation":"이 루프는 \"응답에 text 블록이 있으면 끝\"이라는 텍스트 내용 기반 종료 조건을 쓰고 있습니다. Claude는 한 응답 안에 설명 텍스트와 `tool_use` 블록을 함께 낼 수 있으므로, 도구 요청이 남아 있는데도 루프가 끊겨 고객은 \"확인해 보겠다\"는 말만 듣게 됩니다. 에이전트 루프의 올바른 제어 신호는 `stop_reason`입니다. `\"tool_use\"`이면 도구를 실행하고 tool_result를 붙여 다시 호출하고, `\"end_turn\"`일 때만 종료합니다. 중간 텍스트는 고객에게 보여 줄 수 있지만 종료 판단의 근거가 되어서는 안 됩니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 루프 종료는 자연어 내용이 아니라 `stop_reason`으로 판단 — Task Statement 1.1 · 출처: Section 2 (L5–L6)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 프롬프트로 모델 행동을 바꾸려는 시도일 뿐, 잘못된 종료 조건이라는 근본 원인은 그대로 남습니다.\n- B: 이 응답은 토큰이 모자라서(`max_tokens`) 멈춘 것이 아니라 정상적으로 도구를 요청한 것입니다. 다른 원인을 고치는 답입니다.\n- D: 반복 상한은 안전장치로는 좋지만, 첫 응답에서 바로 `break`되는 이 버그와는 관계가 없습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"text가 있으면 종료\", \"특정 문구가 나오면 종료\"는 모두 안티패턴이고, 정답은 언제나 `stop_reason` 기반 루프입니다.","id":"scenario-a-1","task":"1.1","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":1,"stem":"Harborline's return window is 30 days from delivery. Audits show the agent wrongly denies returns for kiosk orders and wrongly approves some marketplace returns. Investigation finds that `lookup_order` returns delivery dates as Unix epoch seconds for web orders, `\"MM/DD/YY\"` strings for kiosk orders, and ISO 8601 with a timezone offset for marketplace orders; amounts are also mixed between cents and dollars. What is the best way to address this?","options":["Add a detailed section to the system prompt explaining each source system's date and amount formats, with worked examples of converting each one of them correctly.","Register a PostToolUse hook on `lookup_order` that rewrites every result into one canonical shape (ISO dates in UTC, decimal dollars) before Claude sees it.","Give the agent a code-execution tool and instruct it to always compute the day difference and amount conversion in code before deciding on any return.","Ask the three backend teams to change their APIs to a shared format, and route all kiosk and marketplace returns to humans until that work ships."],"answer":1,"explanation":"문제의 근원은 모델의 추론이 아니라 이질적인 도구 결과 형식입니다. Agent SDK의 PostToolUse hook은 도구 실행 직후, 결과가 모델 컨텍스트에 들어가기 전에 가로채서 data normalization을 할 수 있는 결정적인 지점입니다. 여기서 날짜를 UTC ISO 8601로, 금액을 달러 소수로 통일하면 모든 대화에서 같은 형식이 보장되고, 모델은 일관된 데이터 위에서 반품 기한을 판단합니다. 백엔드를 바꾸지 않고도 즉시 적용할 수 있다는 점도 장점입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 형식 차이는 프롬프트가 아니라 hook에서 결정적으로 정규화 — Task Statement 1.5 · 출처: Section 12 (L80), Section 5 (L30)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 프롬프트 설명은 확률적이라 변환 실수가 계속 남습니다. 결정적 처리가 가능한 곳에 프롬프트를 쓰는 함정입니다.\n- C: 계산 정확도는 올라갈 수 있지만, 모델이 형식을 잘못 해석하면(예: MM/DD vs DD/MM) 여전히 틀리고 매번 추가 단계가 필요합니다.\n- D: 장기적으로는 바람직할 수 있지만, 그동안 대량 escalation으로 first-contact resolution 목표를 포기하게 됩니다. 과한 대응입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"여러 소스가 서로 다른 형식을 반환한다\" → PostToolUse hook으로 정규화.","id":"scenario-a-2","task":"1.5","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":1,"stem":"Human specialists report that customers escalated by Tidewater Assist are frustrated because the specialist must re-ask for the order number, re-verify identity, and re-learn what the agent already tried. Currently `escalate_to_human` accepts a single `reason` string and attaches a link to the raw 60-turn transcript. What change would best meet Harborline's handoff goal?","options":["Have the agent fill a structured handoff schema: customer ID, verification status, order IDs and amounts, actions taken with results, blocking reason, and next step.","Attach the full transcript inline to the ticket instead of linking to it, so specialists can read the entire conversation without opening another internal ticketing system.","Ask the agent to write a friendly paragraph summarizing the conversation in the `reason` field, keeping it under two hundred words for quick reading.","Have the agent tell customers before every escalation which details the specialist will need, so they can prepare them in advance for the next conversation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"좋은 handoff payload는 다음 담당자가 대화 기록을 읽지 않고도 바로 일할 수 있게 해 줍니다. 고객 식별자, identity verification 상태, 관련 주문과 금액, 이미 시도한 조치와 결과, 에이전트가 멈춘 이유, 권장 다음 단계를 구조화된 필드로 넘기면 재질문이 사라집니다. 구조화된 필드는 누락 여부를 코드로 검증할 수 있다는 장점도 있습니다. 원문 transcript는 참고용으로 남겨 둘 수 있지만 주된 전달 수단이 되어서는 안 됩니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: handoff = 다음 행위자가 필요한 사실을 담은 구조화 요약 — Task Statement 1.4 · 출처: Section 17 (L115)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 60턴 원문은 정보가 모두 있지만 사람이 핵심을 다시 찾아야 하므로, 재질문 문제는 줄어도 시간 문제는 그대로입니다.\n- C: 자유 서술 요약은 주문 번호나 금액 같은 정확한 값을 빠뜨리거나 흐리기 쉽고, 누락을 검증할 수도 없습니다.\n- D: 부담을 고객에게 넘기는 방식이라 \"고객이 반복하지 않게 한다\"는 목표와 정반대입니다.\n\n시험 팁: escalation 품질 문제 → 원문 전체도, 자유 요약도 아닌 구조화된 handoff 필드.","id":"scenario-a-3","task":"1.4","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":1,"stem":"To enforce the $250 auto-refund limit, the team added a PreToolUse hook that denies any `issue_refund` call whose `amount` exceeds 250. A month later, finance finds several orders refunded $400–$600 in total with no human approval. Each of those orders received two or three separate `issue_refund` calls in the same conversation, each under $250. What is the most effective fix?","options":["Update the system prompt to state that the $250 limit applies to the order as a whole and that splitting one refund into several smaller calls is prohibited.","Lower the per-call threshold in the hook to $125 so that even two split calls on the same order would remain under the overall policy limit.","Add a nightly reconciliation job that compares refunds per order against the limit and claws back or flags any order that went over the cap.","Have the hook look up the order's already-refunded total from the payment ledger and deny when that total plus the new amount exceeds $250, directing escalation."],"answer":3,"explanation":"hook 자체는 올바른 결정적 강제(deterministic enforcement) 수단이지만, 검사하는 값이 틀렸습니다. 정책은 \"주문당 $250\"인데 hook은 \"호출당 금액\"만 보고 있어, 분할 환불로 쉽게 우회됩니다. 근본 원인을 고치려면 hook이 권위 있는 원장(ledger)에서 해당 주문의 누적 환불액을 조회해 새 금액과 합산하고, 한도를 넘으면 거부하면서 `escalate_to_human`을 쓰라는 이유를 Claude에게 돌려줘야 합니다. 대화 기록이 아니라 원장을 기준으로 하므로 여러 세션에 걸친 분할도 막을 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 정책 강제 hook은 정책이 정의한 단위(주문 누적액)를 권위 있는 소스에서 검사해야 함 — Task Statement 1.5 · 출처: Section 5 (L29)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 이미 코드로 강제해야 하는 비가역 금전 정책에 프롬프트를 덧붙이는 것으로, 위반 0건을 보장하지 못합니다.\n- B: 세 번 분할하면 여전히 넘고, 정상적인 $126~$250 단건 환불까지 막아 FCR을 떨어뜨립니다.\n- C: 사후 탐지라 돈은 이미 나갔습니다. 보조 통제는 될 수 있지만 사전 차단을 대신하지 못합니다.\n\n시험 팁: hook이 있는데도 위반이 생기면 \"hook을 버린다\"가 아니라 \"hook이 무엇을 검사하는지\"를 의심하세요.","id":"scenario-a-4","task":"1.5","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":2,"stem":"`commerce-mcp` exposes a single tool, `update_account(field: string, value: string)`, described as \"Updates customer account information.\" When a customer asks to send one pending order to a different address, the agent sometimes sets the `default_shipping_address` field on the account, changing every future order. Occasionally it writes to `billing_address` instead. What is the best redesign?","options":["Split it into purpose-specific tools such as `change_order_address(order_id, address)` and `update_default_address(type, address)`, each stating its scope.","Keep the single tool but change `field` to an enum of allowed field names, so the model can only choose from the documented set of editable customer account fields.","Add a sentence to the system prompt explaining that changes for one order must never be applied to the customer's account-level default shipping address.","Add a confirmation step in which the agent repeats the field name and new value to the customer and waits for a \"yes\" before calling the tool."],"answer":0,"explanation":"문제는 하나의 범용 도구가 서로 다른 의도(주문 단위 변경 vs 계정 기본값 변경)를 모두 덮고 있다는 tool boundary 설계 결함입니다. 목적별 도구로 나누고, 각 설명에 무엇을 하는지, 어떤 입력이 필요한지(`order_id` 필수), 언제 쓰면 안 되는지를 적으면 모델이 의도에 맞는 도구를 고르기 쉬워집니다. 주문 변경 도구는 구조적으로 계정 기본값을 건드릴 수 없으므로 오류의 영향 범위도 줄어듭니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 모호한 범용 도구 → 명확한 경계를 가진 목적별 도구로 분리 — Task Statement 2.1 · 출처: Section 6 (L33–L34)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: enum은 잘못된 필드 이름을 막지만, \"이 주문만 바꿔야 하는데 계정 기본값을 바꾼다\"는 의미상 혼동은 그대로입니다.\n- C: 도구 경계가 모호한 상태에서 프롬프트로만 보정하는 방식이라 신뢰성이 낮습니다.\n- D: 고객은 내부 필드 이름(`default_shipping_address`)의 의미를 판단하기 어렵고, 근본적인 도구 설계 문제를 사람에게 떠넘깁니다.\n\n시험 팁: 하나의 도구가 여러 의도를 받아들이면 enum보다 \"도구 분리 + 경계가 분명한 설명\"이 우선입니다.","id":"scenario-a-5","task":"2.1","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":2,"stem":"During a 20-minute outage of the marketplace order database, Tidewater Assist told dozens of customers that their order \"does not exist in our system\" and suggested they may have ordered from a different retailer. The `lookup_order` tool returns `{\"result\": \"Order lookup failed\"}` for every failure, whether the order ID is unknown, the input is malformed, or the backend times out. What should the team change first?","options":["Add a system prompt instruction telling the agent to retry `lookup_order` three times with a short delay before telling a customer that an order cannot be found.","Return `isError: true` with a category (not_found, invalid_input, backend_unavailable), an `isRetryable` flag, and a short message describing what happened.","Wrap `lookup_order` in a circuit breaker so that during outages the tool stops calling the database and returns cached order data instead.","Have the MCP server raise an exception on any failure so the SDK aborts the session and the customer is moved to the human queue."],"answer":1,"explanation":"모델은 도구가 준 정보만으로 판단합니다. \"실패했다\"는 한 가지 메시지로는 주문이 없는 것과 시스템이 일시적으로 응답하지 않는 것을 구분할 수 없으므로, 모델이 가장 그럴듯한 해석(\"주문 없음\")을 고객에게 말한 것입니다. MCP 도구 결과에 `isError`를 설정하고 error category, retryable 여부, 설명 메시지를 담으면, 에이전트가 일시 장애 시에는 사과와 재시도 또는 escalation을, not_found일 때만 주문 정보 재확인을 선택할 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 구조화된 오류 응답 = 실패 유형 구분 + 재시도 가능 여부 + 맥락 — Task Statement 2.2 · 출처: Section 6 (L37), Section 7 (L46)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 오류 유형을 모르는 채 무조건 재시도하면, 진짜 not_found나 잘못된 입력에서도 헛되이 반복합니다. 구분 정보가 여전히 없습니다.\n- C: circuit breaker는 장애 대응에 유용하지만, 오류를 구분하는 문제를 해결하지 못하고 오래된 캐시를 정답처럼 보여 줄 위험도 있습니다.\n- D: 모든 실패를 세션 중단으로 처리하면 단순 입력 오류에도 대화가 끝나 FCR이 크게 떨어집니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"에이전트가 장애를 '없음'으로 해석했다\" → 구조화된 오류(category + retryable)가 1순위입니다.","id":"scenario-a-6","task":"2.2","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":2,"stem":"Harborline's routing design requires that the very first model call in each conversation invoke `classify_intent`, whose output selects the policy pack loaded for the rest of the chat. With default settings, the agent sometimes greets the customer or calls `lookup_order` first, and the policy pack never loads. Later turns must remain free to answer in text or call any tool. What is the best configuration?","options":["Set `tool_choice` to `{\"type\": \"any\"}` on every request so that each model turn must produce a tool call and cannot skip classification.","Move `classify_intent` to the top of the tools array and state in its description that it must always be called first in every new customer conversation.","Use `tool_choice: {\"type\": \"tool\", \"name\": \"classify_intent\"}` for the first call only, then switch to `{\"type\": \"auto\"}` for every later turn.","Remove all other tools from the first request so that `classify_intent` is the only tool available and keep `tool_choice` set to `auto`."],"answer":2,"explanation":"반드시 일어나야 하는 특정 고정 단계는 `tool_choice`를 `{\"type\": \"tool\", \"name\": ...}`로 지정해 결정적으로 강제합니다. 이후 턴은 텍스트 응답과 자유로운 도구 선택이 모두 가능해야 하므로 `auto`로 돌려놓습니다. 이렇게 하면 첫 단계의 신뢰성과 이후 대화의 유연성을 둘 다 얻습니다. 참고로 `tool_choice` 변경은 캐시된 message 블록을 무효화할 수 있지만, 첫 호출에서만 바꾸므로 영향이 작습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 특정 도구를 반드시 먼저 → forced tool choice, 그 뒤 auto — Task Statement 2.3 · 출처: Section 6 (L41)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: `any`는 \"어떤 도구든\" 하나를 강제하므로 `lookup_order`가 먼저 호출될 수 있고, 이후 텍스트 답변까지 막습니다.\n- B: 배열 순서와 설명 문구는 선택 확률을 높일 뿐 보장하지 못합니다.\n- D: 도구가 하나뿐이어도 `auto`에서는 모델이 텍스트(인사)만 내고 도구를 호출하지 않을 수 있습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"항상 이 도구를 먼저\" → `tool`, \"어떤 도구든 반드시\" → `any`, \"텍스트만\" → `none`.","id":"scenario-a-7","task":"2.3","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":2,"stem":"To simplify configuration, the coordinator and the billing-dispute subagent were both given the full set of 19 `commerce-mcp` tools. Since then, the subagent, which should only investigate charges and report findings, has occasionally issued refunds and cancelled orders mid-investigation, and the coordinator sometimes calls `get_processor_charges` directly with incomplete parameters instead of delegating. What is the best way to address this?","options":["Add a sentence to each agent's system prompt listing which tools it is responsible for and asking it not to use tools belonging to the other agent.","Merge the subagent back into the coordinator so a single agent owns all 19 tools and there is no confusion about who performs each action.","Keep the full tool set but add a PreToolUse hook that logs every cross-role tool call so the team can review misuse patterns weekly.","Scope tools per role: give the subagent read-only charge and order lookups plus a findings tool, and keep refunds and processor calls with their owners."],"answer":3,"explanation":"각 에이전트에게 역할에 필요한 도구만 주는 것이 tool distribution의 기본 원칙입니다. 도구가 많을수록 선택 정확도가 떨어지고, 역할 밖 도구가 있으면 서브에이전트가 범위를 넘어 비가역적 조치(환불, 취소)를 할 수 있습니다. 조사 전용 서브에이전트에는 읽기 전용 조회 도구와 결과 보고 도구만, 프로세서 조회는 서브에이전트에게, 환불은 정책 검사를 거치는 쪽에 두면 실수가 구조적으로 불가능해지고 위임도 자연스럽게 일어납니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: least privilege — 역할별로 도구 집합을 최소화 — Task Statement 2.3 · 출처: Section 6 (L39)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 도구가 여전히 존재하므로 프롬프트 지시만으로는 비가역 조치를 막지 못합니다.\n- B: 하나의 에이전트에 19개 도구를 몰아주면 선택 오류는 오히려 늘고, 조사 맥락이 고객 대화 맥락을 오염시킵니다.\n- C: 로깅은 사후 관찰일 뿐 오용을 막지 않습니다. 이미 일어난 환불은 되돌릴 수 없습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"에이전트가 자기 역할 밖 도구를 쓴다\" → 프롬프트가 아니라 도구 목록 자체를 줄이세요.","id":"scenario-a-8","task":"2.3","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":4,"stem":"The QA reviewer prompt says: \"Review this transcript and flag any policy violations, unprofessional language, or legal risk.\" Supervisors find that about 40% of flags are false positives, such as flagging \"I'm sorry this happened\" as an admission of liability and flagging correct $250 refunds as \"excessive.\" Agents have started ignoring the reports. What is the most effective improvement?","options":["Define each flag category with explicit criteria and concrete examples of what does and does not count, and pause categories whose precision stays low.","Tell the reviewer to be conservative and only flag issues it is highly confident about, and to skip anything it considers minor, borderline, or open to interpretation.","Ask the reviewer to attach a 0–1 confidence score to every flag and only show supervisors flags with a self-reported confidence above 0.8.","Run the reviewer three times per transcript and only report flags that appear in at least two of the three independent review passes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"false positive의 원인은 \"policy violation\", \"legal risk\" 같은 모호한 기준입니다. 모델은 각 범주의 경계를 모르니 공감 표현을 책임 인정으로, 한도 내 환불을 과도한 환불로 해석합니다. 범주마다 explicit criteria(예: \"법적 책임 인정 = 과실을 명시적으로 인정하는 문장, 단순 사과는 제외\", \"환불 과다 = 주문당 누적 $250 초과\")와 포함·제외 예시를 주면 precision이 올라갑니다. 기준을 다듬는 동안 정밀도가 낮은 범주는 잠시 끄는 것이 리뷰 결과에 대한 신뢰를 되찾는 데 효과적입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 모호한 지시 대신 명시적 판정 기준으로 false positive 감소 — Task Statement 4.1 · 출처: Section 13 (L83–L84)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: \"보수적으로\", \"확실한 것만\" 같은 지시도 모호합니다. 기준이 없으니 정밀도는 거의 개선되지 않고 진짜 위반도 놓칠 수 있습니다.\n- C: 모델의 self-reported confidence는 보정되지 않아, 확신에 찬 오판을 걸러내지 못합니다.\n- D: 같은 모호한 기준으로 여러 번 돌리면 같은 오해가 반복되어 다수결로도 걸러지지 않습니다. 비용만 세 배입니다.\n\n시험 팁: false positive가 많다 → 먼저 \"무엇이 해당하고 무엇이 해당하지 않는지\"를 명시하세요.","id":"scenario-a-9","task":"4.1","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":4,"stem":"At the end of each conversation, the CRM integration needs a case record with `disposition` (one of five values), `refund_amount`, `order_ids`, and `escalated` (boolean). The current prompt ends with \"Reply with the case record as JSON.\" About 6% of outputs fail to parse because of leading prose or markdown fences, and some contain invented dispositions like `\"partially_resolved\"`. What is the best approach?","options":["Add three few-shot examples of correctly formatted case records to the prompt and strip markdown fences with a regex before parsing the output.","Parse the output with a lenient JSON parser and map any unknown disposition to the closest valid value using string-similarity matching.","Define a `record_case_outcome` tool with a JSON schema (`disposition` as an enum), force it with `tool_choice`, and read the tool_use input.","Add a validation step that sends malformed records back to the model with the parse error and asks it to output corrected JSON."],"answer":2,"explanation":"후속 시스템이 바로 받아 써야 하는 정형 데이터라면 tool use + JSON schema로 출력을 받는 것이 가장 안정적입니다. 도구의 `input_schema`에 `disposition`을 enum으로, `escalated`를 boolean으로 정의하고, `tool_choice`로 그 도구를 강제하면 산문이나 코드 펜스가 섞일 여지가 사라집니다. 결과는 `tool_use` 블록의 `input`에서 구조화된 객체로 읽습니다. 여기에 `strict: true`까지 쓰면 schema 준수가 보장되어 허용되지 않은 enum 값도 막을 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 신뢰할 수 있는 구조화 출력 = 도구 스키마 + 강제 호출 — Task Statement 4.3 · 출처: Section 15 (L97, L100)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: few-shot과 정규식은 실패율을 낮출 뿐 형식과 enum 준수를 보장하지 못합니다.\n- B: 문자열 유사도로 값을 바꾸면 모델이 만든 의미를 몰래 바꾸게 되어 데이터 오류를 숨깁니다.\n- D: 재시도 루프는 의미 검증에는 유용하지만, 형식 실패는 처음부터 schema로 막는 것이 더 근본적입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"JSON으로 답하라\"는 프롬프트 + 파싱 실패 → 정답은 tool_use와 JSON schema(필요하면 strict)입니다.","id":"scenario-a-10","task":"4.3","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":5,"stem":"A customer spends 70 turns resolving three issues. Early on, the agent and customer agreed on a $83.40 partial refund for order HB-55102 and confirmed the customer wants store credit rather than a card refund. After automatic context compaction, the agent issues $80 to the card, citing \"the agreed partial refund.\" The compaction summary reads: \"Customer received partial refund agreement for a jacket order.\" What is the most effective fix?","options":["Increase the compaction threshold so summarization happens much later in the conversation, keeping more of the original verbatim turns available to the agent later.","Tell the summarizer in its prompt to be thorough and include all important details, especially any dollar amounts, order IDs, and stated customer preferences.","Maintain a structured case-facts block (order IDs, agreed amounts, refund method, verification status) outside the summarized history, re-injected every turn.","Before any refund, have the agent ask the customer to restate the order number, the agreed amount, and their preferred refund method."],"answer":2,"explanation":"요약은 본질적으로 정보를 압축하므로 정확한 숫자, 식별자, 선호 사항이 \"부분 환불 합의\" 같은 흐릿한 표현으로 바뀌기 쉽습니다. 금액과 주문 번호처럼 정확해야 하는 사실은 요약 대상에서 빼고, persistent fact block(case facts)으로 구조화해 매 턴 컨텍스트에 그대로 다시 넣어야 합니다. 이렇게 하면 compaction이 몇 번 일어나도 $83.40, HB-55102, store credit 같은 값이 손실 없이 유지됩니다. fact block은 도구 결과나 합의 시점에 갱신합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 정확해야 하는 사실은 요약하지 말고 별도 구조화 블록으로 보존 — Task Statement 5.1 · 출처: Section 16 (L109–L110)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 손실 시점을 늦출 뿐이고, 긴 대화에서는 결국 같은 손실이 일어납니다. 비용과 지연도 늘어납니다.\n- B: 요약 프롬프트를 개선해도 요약은 확률적이라 정확한 값의 보존을 보장하지 못합니다.\n- D: 고객에게 반복을 요구해 경험을 해치고, 고객이 다르게 기억하면 새로운 불일치까지 생깁니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"요약 후 숫자·ID·선호가 사라졌다\" → case facts 블록이 정답입니다.","id":"scenario-a-11","task":"5.1","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":5,"stem":"A customer shows a competitor's listing and asks Harborline to match a lower price on a tent bought six days ago. Harborline's policy document covers price adjustments when Harborline itself lowers a price within 14 days, but says nothing about competitor prices. The customer is calm and polite. Transcripts show the agent handles this inconsistently: sometimes it refuses, sometimes it applies a \"goodwill\" refund for the difference. What should the agent do?","options":["Treat it as a policy gap: explain that this request needs review, then escalate with the listing, order details, and the relevant policy section.","Apply the price adjustment rule by analogy, since a competitor price match serves the same customer-retention purpose as an own-store price drop.","Decline the request politely, because the policy document does not authorize competitor price matching and the agent must stay within it.","Offer a smaller goodwill credit as a compromise, keeping the amount well under the $250 limit so the case can be resolved without any handoff to a specialist."],"answer":0,"explanation":"이 사례는 고객 감정이나 금액 문제가 아니라 정책이 침묵하는(policy gap) 경우입니다. Harborline 규칙은 정책에 없는 요청을 사람에게 보내라고 정하고 있으며, 이런 진짜 모호한 경우가 바로 escalation trigger가 다뤄야 할 대상입니다. 에이전트가 유추로 승인하거나 임의로 거절하면 정책이 일관되지 않게 적용되고, 실제로 transcript에서 그 문제가 드러났습니다. 근거 자료(경쟁사 페이지, 주문, 관련 정책 조항)를 담아 넘기면 사람이 빠르게 판단할 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 정책이 다루지 않는 요청 → 에이전트 임의 판단이 아니라 escalation — Task Statement 5.2 · 출처: Section 17 (L114)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 유추로 정책 범위를 넓히는 것은 에이전트가 가져서는 안 되는 판단 권한을 행사하는 것입니다.\n- C: \"명시적 허용이 없으면 거절\"은 정책에 없는 영역을 에이전트가 대신 결정하는 것이며, 회사 규칙(정책 밖 요청은 사람에게)과도 어긋납니다.\n- D: 한도 내 금액이라도 근거 없는 보상은 정책 위반이며, 금액 한도는 정책 공백을 메우는 권한이 아닙니다.\n\n시험 팁: escalation 조건은 감정이 아니라 \"정책 공백, 명시적 사람 요청, 진전 불가\"입니다.","id":"scenario-a-12","task":"5.2","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":5,"stem":"Today a human samples 20% of all agent-resolved cases. Operations proposes to stop sampling any case in which the agent's self-reported confidence is at least 0.9, which covers 85% of cases. Overall accuracy on last month's sampled cases was 97%, but the team has never broken accuracy down by case type. Billing disputes are 6% of volume. What should the team do before reducing human review?","options":["Measure accuracy by case type and confidence band on a labeled set, and keep stratified sampling so rare, high-impact types like billing disputes stay reviewed.","Approve the proposal, since 97% overall accuracy combined with a 0.9 confidence cutoff gives strong evidence the high-confidence cases are safe to skip entirely.","Raise the cutoff to 0.95 so that fewer cases skip review, and then compare the overall accuracy of the remaining sampled cases month over month to confirm.","Ask the agent to explain its reasoning for each high-confidence case so supervisors can skim explanations instead of auditing full transcripts."],"answer":0,"explanation":"전체 정확도 97%는 대부분을 차지하는 쉬운 사례가 끌어올린 수치일 수 있고, 비중 6%인 billing dispute처럼 드물지만 영향이 큰 유형의 오류를 가릴 수 있습니다. 또 모델의 self-reported confidence는 실제 정확도와 맞춰 calibration하기 전까지 신뢰할 수 없습니다. 먼저 레이블된 검증 세트로 유형별, 신뢰 구간별 정확도를 측정해 confidence가 정말 정확도를 예측하는지 확인하고, 이후에도 stratified sampling으로 소수 유형을 계속 검토해야 합니다. 그 결과를 근거로 안전한 구간에서만 검토를 줄입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 집계 정확도는 세그먼트 오류를 숨김 → 보정 + 층화 표본으로 검토 축소 결정 — Task Statement 5.5 · 출처: Section 19 (L127–L128)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 보정되지 않은 confidence와 집계 정확도만으로 검토를 없애는, 이 문제가 겨냥하는 바로 그 함정입니다.\n- C: 기준값만 바꾸고 보정하지 않으니 여전히 근거가 없고, 전체 정확도 비교로는 세그먼트 문제가 계속 숨겨집니다.\n- D: 모델의 설명은 그럴듯하게 쓰일 수 있어 정확성 검증을 대신하지 못하며, 검토 대상 선정 문제도 풀지 못합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"전체 정확도가 높으니 자동화\" → 유형별 분석, calibration, stratified sampling을 먼저 떠올리세요.","id":"scenario-a-13","task":"5.5","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":5,"stem":"A customer says they were charged twice for one order. The coordinator delegates to the billing-dispute subagent, which calls `get_processor_charges`. The processor API returns HTTP 503 twice; the subagent's wrapper catches the exception and returns `{\"charges\": [], \"duplicates_found\": false}`. The coordinator then tells the customer, \"I've confirmed there is only one charge on your card,\" and closes the case. What is the best fix?","options":["Instruct the coordinator to always run its own second check against the payment processor before telling a customer that no duplicate charges were found.","Increase the subagent's retry budget to ten attempts with exponential backoff so that short processor outages no longer cause empty results.","Have the subagent escalate directly to a human whenever any tool call fails, bypassing the coordinator so that it never receives or relays an incomplete result.","Make the subagent return a status that separates \"query failed\" from \"no results,\" with error details and what was attempted, so the coordinator can decide."],"answer":3,"explanation":"이것은 전형적인 silent failure입니다. wrapper가 오류를 빈 결과로 바꾸면서 \"조회 실패\"와 \"조회 성공, 결과 없음\"이 같은 모양이 되었고, coordinator는 이를 확인된 사실로 믿었습니다. 서브에이전트는 오류를 숨기지 말고 구조화된 상태(success / failed / partial), 오류 유형, 시도한 내용, 부분 결과를 반환해 실패를 위로 전파(propagate)해야 합니다. 그래야 coordinator가 고객에게 정직하게 알리고, 재시도나 escalation 중 무엇을 할지 맥락을 바탕으로 결정할 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: \"아무것도 없음\"과 \"확인 못 함\"을 구분하는 propagation contract — Task Statement 5.3 · 출처: Section 17 (L117–L118)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 근본 원인인 오류 은폐를 그대로 두고 중복 작업만 늘립니다. coordinator의 재조회도 같은 장애를 만날 수 있습니다.\n- B: 재시도는 일시 장애를 줄일 수 있지만, 예산이 바닥나면 여전히 빈 결과로 위장됩니다.\n- C: 서브에이전트가 coordinator를 우회하면 대화 소유자가 상황을 모르게 되어, 고객 응대와 handoff가 꼬입니다.\n\n시험 팁: 빈 결과가 의심스러우면 \"실패를 성공처럼 보이게 만든 지점\"을 찾으세요. 정답은 구조화된 오류 전파입니다.","id":"scenario-a-14","task":"5.3","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":5,"stem":"A customer chatting as a guest writes, \"This is Dana Whitfield, I need to change the email on my account.\" `get_account` returns three active accounts named Dana Whitfield in different states. Logs show the agent usually selects the account with the most recent order and proceeds to identity verification for that account. What should the agent do instead?","options":["Select the account whose region matches the IP geolocation of the current chat session, since that is the strongest available signal of the customer's location.","Escalate every case with more than one name match to a human specialist, since account changes on the wrong customer would be a serious privacy incident.","Ask the customer for an identifier that separates the matches, such as an order number or the current account email, before running verification.","Show the customer the three accounts' masked emails and cities so they can pick which one is theirs, then continue with verification for that one."],"answer":2,"explanation":"조회 결과가 여러 건일 때 에이전트가 휴리스틱(최근 주문, 지역 등)으로 하나를 고르면, 다른 고객의 계정을 대상으로 작업할 위험이 있습니다. 올바른 ambiguity resolution은 고객에게 매칭을 확실히 구분할 수 있는 추가 식별자(주문 번호, 계정 이메일 등)를 요청하는 것입니다. 고객 입력으로 하나로 좁힌 뒤 그 계정에 대해 신원 확인을 진행하면, 정확도와 개인정보 보호, first-contact resolution을 모두 지킬 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 다중 매칭 → 추측하지 말고 구분 가능한 식별자를 요청 — Task Statement 5.2 · 출처: Section 17 (L119)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: IP 위치도 휴리스틱일 뿐이라 여행 중이거나 VPN을 쓰는 고객이면 틀립니다. 추측이라는 점은 그대로입니다.\n- B: 고객이 직접 풀 수 있는 모호성까지 사람에게 넘기면 FCR 목표를 불필요하게 해칩니다.\n- D: 다른 고객들의 부분 정보(이메일, 도시)를 확인되지 않은 사용자에게 노출하는 개인정보 문제가 생깁니다.\n\n시험 팁: 동명이인 등 다중 매칭 → \"가장 그럴듯한 것 선택\"이 아니라 \"추가 식별자 요청\".","id":"scenario-a-15","task":"5.2","scenario":"Customer Support Resolution Agent","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Outfitters is a mid-sized online retailer of outdoor gear that has replaced its tier-1 chat queue with Tidewater Assist, a customer support agent built on the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator agent talks to the customer and can delegate to a billing-dispute subagent that investigates card charges with the payment processor. Both agents reach backend systems through an internal MCP server, `commerce-mcp`, which exposes tools such as `verify_identity`, `get_account`, `lookup_order`, `issue_refund`, `cancel_order`, `open_billing_dispute`, `get_processor_charges`, and `escalate_to_human`. Company policy allows the agent to refund up to $250 per order on its own; anything above that, any chargeback already filed with a bank, and any request the written policy does not cover must go to a human specialist through `escalate_to_human`. Order data comes from three legacy systems (web store, marketplace partner, and in-store kiosk) that format dates, currencies, and amounts differently. Conversations often span several issues and run for dozens of turns, and the context is compacted automatically when it grows long. Harborline's goals are 80% first-contact resolution, zero refunds that violate policy, and human handoffs that never force the customer to repeat themselves. A separate Claude-based QA reviewer scores finished transcripts, and the operations team is considering letting the agent auto-approve more cases without human sampling."},{"domain":3,"stem":"Senior engineer Mina added the rule \"All new API handlers must return `Result<T, AppError>` and must never throw\" to her `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` a month ago. Handlers generated in her sessions comply. This week, three new hires generated handlers in `services/quote/` that throw exceptions, and nobody saw any error or warning. What is the most likely root cause?","options":["The project `CLAUDE.md` contains an opposing rule, and the more specific project file always wins over a user-level file.","The rule lives in Mina's user-level file, which loads only in her own sessions and never reaches other contributors.","The new hires launched Claude Code from a subdirectory, so every memory file above that folder was skipped at startup.","User-level instructions only take effect after `/init` is rerun in each repository, which the new hires never did."],"answer":1,"explanation":"`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`는 user-level 메모리로, 그 파일을 가진 사람의 세션에만 로드됩니다. 팀 표준을 user 파일에 두면 오류나 경고 없이 조용히 실패(silent failure)합니다. Mina의 세션은 정상으로 보이므로 원인을 찾기도 어렵습니다. 팀 전체가 따라야 하는 규칙은 저장소에 커밋된 project-level `CLAUDE.md`에 두어야 모든 기여자가 같은 지시를 받습니다. 문제의 핵심은 \"누구를 위한 지시인가(audience)\"에 맞는 scope를 고르지 못한 것입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 팀 표준 → 커밋된 project CLAUDE.md, 개인 선호 → user CLAUDE.md — Task Statement 3.1 · 출처: Section 10 (L63, L64)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: CLAUDE.md 사이에는 \"더 구체적인 파일이 항상 이긴다\"는 신뢰할 수 있는 precedence가 없으며, 지문에 반대 규칙이 있다는 근거도 없습니다.\n- C: 하위 디렉터리에서 시작해도 상위 디렉터리의 CLAUDE.md는 로드됩니다. 또 user 파일은 위치와 무관하게 해당 사용자에게만 로드됩니다.\n- D: `/init`은 starter CLAUDE.md를 생성하는 명령일 뿐, user-level 파일 활성화 조건이 아닙니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"내 세션만 정상, 남의 세션은 조용히 다름\" → 팀 규칙이 user scope에 있는지 먼저 의심하세요.","id":"scenario-a-16","task":"3.1","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":3,"stem":"Atlas has strict testing conventions: use factory helpers from `@corvane/testkit`, never hit the real network, and name cases `it(\"should …\")`. Test files sit next to their sources everywhere, for example `services/quote/rate.test.ts` and `web/src/cart/Cart.test.tsx`. The conventions currently live in the root `CLAUDE.md`, where they consume context in every session, including sessions that never touch tests. What is the best way to apply these conventions?","options":["Add a `CLAUDE.md` inside every directory that contains test files, each one holding a copy of the testing conventions.","Create `.claude/rules/testing.md` with `paths` frontmatter globs such as `**/*.test.ts` and `**/*.test.tsx`.","Move the conventions into a `/write-tests` skill so they are loaded whenever a developer explicitly invokes it.","Keep them in the root `CLAUDE.md` under a \"Testing\" heading so Claude applies that section only to test files."],"answer":1,"explanation":"이 관례는 특정 폴더가 아니라 파일 유형(테스트 파일)을 따라다니며, 테스트 파일은 저장소 전체에 흩어져 있습니다. `.claude/rules/` 아래 규칙 파일에 `paths` frontmatter로 glob을 지정하면 일치하는 파일을 Claude가 읽을 때만 conditional loading되어, 테스트와 무관한 세션의 컨텍스트를 아끼면서 필요한 순간에 정확히 적용됩니다. ``는 디렉터리 깊이와 무관하게 매칭하므로 colocated 테스트를 모두 포괄합니다. \"Convention follows the folder → subdirectory CLAUDE.md, convention follows the file type → path-scoped rule\"이 결정 규칙입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 폴더를 가로지르는 파일 유형별 관례 → `.claude/rules/` + `paths` glob — Task Statement 3.3 · 출처: Section 10 (L67)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 동작은 하지만 수십 개 복사본이 생겨 유지보수 부채와 drift가 발생합니다. 폴더 단위 관례에 맞는 도구를 파일 유형 관례에 잘못 쓴 경우입니다.\n- C: skill은 on-demand 절차용입니다. 테스트 파일을 만질 때마다 지켜야 할 상시 관례를 명시적 호출에 의존하게 만들면 누락됩니다.\n- D: Markdown heading은 로딩 범위를 정하지 못합니다. 여전히 매 세션 전체가 로드됩니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"여러 디렉터리에 흩어진 같은 종류의 파일\" → path-scoped rule이 정답 패턴입니다.","id":"scenario-a-17","task":"3.3","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":3,"stem":"The team's `/audit-deps` skill reads lockfiles from 30 packages, runs `npm ls` repeatedly, and walks through thousands of lines of output before producing a short upgrade recommendation. After running it, developers notice that the main session is cluttered with dependency output and Claude starts losing track of instructions given earlier in the conversation. Which change best addresses this?","options":["Add `context: fork` to the skill's frontmatter so it runs in an isolated subagent and returns only its final summary.","Add `allowed-tools: Read, Grep` to the frontmatter so the skill can no longer flood the session with verbose Bash output.","Move the skill from `.claude/skills/` to `~/.claude/skills/` so its output stays inside each developer's personal context.","Set `disable-model-invocation: true` so that the skill's tool output is excluded from the main conversation history."],"answer":0,"explanation":"문제의 본질은 장황한 탐색 출력이 메인 세션의 컨텍스트를 오염시키는 것입니다. Skill frontmatter의 `context: fork`는 skill을 격리된 subagent 컨텍스트에서 실행하게 하므로, 수천 줄의 중간 출력은 그쪽에 머물고 메인 세션에는 요약 결과만 돌아옵니다. 이것이 context isolation을 활용해 메인 대화의 지시와 맥락을 보존하는 방법입니다. 필요하면 `agent` 필드로 어떤 subagent가 처리할지도 지정할 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 장황한 출력을 내는 skill → `context: fork`로 격리 실행 — Task Statement 3.2 · 출처: Section 11 (L74, L75)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: `allowed-tools`는 나열한 도구를 사전 승인할 뿐 다른 도구를 제거하지 않습니다. 또 Read/Grep 출력도 여전히 메인 컨텍스트를 채웁니다.\n- C: 저장 위치(scope)는 누가 그 skill을 쓸 수 있는지를 정할 뿐, 실행 컨텍스트 격리와 무관합니다.\n- D: `disable-model-invocation`은 Claude가 자동으로 호출하지 못하게 할 뿐, 출력이 대화에 남는 것은 그대로입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"skill 실행 후 메인 컨텍스트가 지저분해짐\" → `context: fork`를 떠올리세요.","id":"scenario-a-18","task":"3.2","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":3,"stem":"A tech lead is deciding which of this sprint's tasks should start in plan mode rather than direct execution. Which task most clearly warrants plan mode?","options":["Correct a misspelled word in a single user-facing error message that QA flagged in one handler file.","Add a null check to one function where the stack trace already points to the exact failing line.","Replace the in-house event bus with the new queue library across 45 files in three services.","Rename one local variable inside a single utility function so it matches the team naming guide."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Plan mode는 파일을 쓰지 않는 read-only 단계에서 코드베이스를 탐색하고 단계, 대상 파일, 위험을 담은 제안서를 승인 관문(approval gate) 앞에 내놓습니다. 45개 파일과 세 서비스에 걸친 라이브러리 교체는 multi-file, 아키텍처 결정, 되돌리기 어려운 변경이라는 조건을 모두 갖추어 사전 계획의 가치가 가장 큽니다. 실행 전에 모든 접점과 순서를 드러내면 중간에 잘못된 방향을 발견해 대량 재작업하는 비용을 피할 수 있습니다. 나머지 세 작업은 범위가 명확한 단일 파일 변경이라 direct execution이 더 빠릅니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 여러 모듈에 걸치거나 되돌리기 어려우면 plan mode, 작고 명확하고 되돌릴 수 있으면 direct execution — Task Statement 3.4 · 출처: Section 11 (L78, L79)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 단일 파일의 오타 수정은 기계적 변경이라 승인 관문의 오버헤드가 이득보다 큽니다.\n- B: stack trace가 정확한 위치를 알려 주는 단일 수정은 명확한 범위의 direct execution 대상입니다.\n- D: 지역 변수 하나의 이름 변경은 영향 범위가 함수 내부에 국한되어 즉시 실행이 적합합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"10초에 되돌릴 실수인가, 30분이 걸릴 실수인가\"로 plan mode 여부를 판단하세요.","id":"scenario-a-19","task":"3.4","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":3,"stem":"A developer new to the pricing domain asks Claude to build a carrier-tariff cache for the quoting API. On two earlier attempts, Claude assumed simple TTL expiry and per-region caches, but reviewers rejected both because tariffs must be invalidated the moment a carrier publishes a change and quotes must be consistent across regions. Neither requirement was written down anywhere. What is the most effective approach for the next attempt?","options":["Expand the prompt with an exhaustive list of caching best practices so Claude can pick the most suitable strategy itself.","Ask Claude to interview the developer first, raising design questions such as invalidation triggers and consistency needs.","Let Claude implement right away, then reply \"this is wrong, try again\" after each review until a reviewer finally approves.","Switch to auto-accept edits so that each attempt finishes faster, and gather all of the review feedback at the very end."],"answer":1,"explanation":"실패의 원인은 코드 품질이 아니라 명시되지 않은 요구사항을 Claude가 가정으로 채운 것입니다. 개발자 자신도 익숙하지 않은 도메인에서는 Claude가 먼저 질문하게 하는 interview pattern이 효과적입니다. Claude는 무효화 트리거, 지역 간 일관성, 장애 시 동작처럼 개발자가 미처 생각하지 못한 설계 고려사항을 표면화하고, 답을 받은 뒤 구현에 들어갑니다. 구현 후 고치는 것보다 사전에 모호성을 해소하는 것이 훨씬 저렴하며, 이는 iterative refinement의 출발점입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 낯선 도메인·숨은 요구사항 → 구현 전에 Claude가 인터뷰하게 하여 가정을 드러냄 — Task Statement 3.5 · 출처: Section 14 (L95), Section 11 (L78)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 일반적인 모범 사례 목록은 이 프로젝트 고유의 숨은 요구사항을 알려 주지 못하고 컨텍스트만 늘립니다.\n- C: 구체적 근거 없는 \"다시 해\" 피드백은 무엇이 틀렸는지 전달하지 못해 같은 가정을 반복하게 합니다.\n- D: 실행 속도를 높여도 잘못된 가정이라는 근본 원인은 그대로이며, 재작업 비용만 뒤로 미룹니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"요구사항이 어디에도 적혀 있지 않았다\" → 구현 전 interview/clarification이 정답 방향입니다.","id":"scenario-a-20","task":"3.5","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":2,"stem":"The platform team wants every engineer who clones Atlas to have the `corvane-tickets` MCP server available in Claude Code automatically. The server is reached over Streamable HTTP and requires each engineer's personal API token. Security policy forbids committing credentials to the repository. Which configuration best meets these requirements?","options":["Have each engineer run `claude mcp add` at user scope and paste their own token directly into the command line.","Commit `.mcp.json` with a shared token embedded in it, and restrict repository read access to the platform team only.","Document the server URL in the root `CLAUDE.md` so Claude connects to it whenever a ticket number is mentioned.","Commit a project-scoped `.mcp.json` that references the token as `${TICKETS_API_TOKEN}` from each engineer's environment."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Claude Code에서 project scope MCP 설정은 저장소 루트의 `.mcp.json`에 두고 커밋하므로, clone한 모든 엔지니어가 별도 작업 없이 같은 서버 구성을 공유합니다. `.mcp.json`은 환경 변수 확장(`${VAR}`)을 지원하므로 토큰 값 자체는 각자의 환경에 두고 파일에는 참조만 남길 수 있습니다. 이렇게 하면 \"팀 전체 자동 공유\"와 \"자격 증명 미커밋\"이라는 두 요구를 동시에 충족합니다. 프로젝트 범위 서버는 처음 사용할 때 승인 확인을 거친다는 점도 알아 두세요.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 팀 공유 MCP = 커밋된 `.mcp.json`, 비밀값 = `${ENV_VAR}` 확장 — Task Statement 2.4 · 출처: Section 7 (L49 보충 S4), Section 8 (L55)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: user scope는 개인용 설정이라 저장소로 공유되지 않고, 엔지니어마다 수동 설정이 필요해 \"자동\" 요구를 충족하지 못합니다.\n- B: 접근 제한과 무관하게 자격 증명을 커밋하는 것은 정책 위반이며 공유 토큰은 감사 추적도 흐립니다.\n- C: CLAUDE.md는 지시문일 뿐 MCP 서버 연결을 구성하는 메커니즘이 아닙니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"팀 공유 + 비밀 미커밋\" 조합이 보이면 `.mcp.json` + `${VAR}`를 고르세요.","id":"scenario-a-21","task":"2.4","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":3,"stem":"`infra/CLAUDE.md` contains: \"Never run `terraform apply`. Never delete or rename `aws_db_instance` resources.\" A developer opens a session at the repository root, immediately runs `/memory`, and sees the root `CLAUDE.md` and their user file listed, but not `infra/CLAUDE.md`. They conclude the infra file is broken and propose moving its rules into the root file. What is the correct assessment?","options":["The infra file is ignored because subdirectory `CLAUDE.md` files must first be registered through an `@import` line in the root file.","The infra file is broken, since subdirectory files load only when the Claude Code session is launched from inside that directory.","The infra file will override the root `CLAUDE.md` once it loads, so keeping it out of startup is what protects the root rules.","This is expected, since subdirectory files load lazily once Claude reads files in `infra/`, and then add to the root rules."],"answer":3,"explanation":"하위 디렉터리의 `CLAUDE.md`는 세션 시작 시가 아니라 Claude가 그 디렉터리 안의 파일을 읽는 순간 lazy load됩니다. 따라서 세션 직후 `/memory`에 보이지 않는 것은 정상 동작이며, Terraform 파일을 읽으면 그때 로드됩니다. 로드된 하위 파일은 부모 지시를 대체하지 않고 그 위에 augment(추가)됩니다. 위험한 제약을 보호 대상 코드 바로 옆에 두는 현재 구조가 오히려 권장 패턴이므로, root로 옮기면 모든 세션에 불필요한 컨텍스트만 늘어납니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: subdirectory CLAUDE.md = 읽기 시점 lazy load + additive layering — Task Statement 3.1 · 출처: Section 10 (L65, L64)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 하위 CLAUDE.md는 위치 자체가 범위이며 등록이나 manifest 단계가 없습니다. `@import`는 모듈화 수단이지 활성화 조건이 아닙니다.\n- B: 그 디렉터리에서 시작해도 로드되지만 \"그때만\"이 아닙니다. 루트 세션에서도 해당 파일을 읽으면 로드됩니다.\n- C: 하위 파일은 부모를 override하지 않고 덧붙여지며, 충돌 시 신뢰할 수 있는 승자도 없습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"시작 직후 목록에 없음\"만으로 고장이라 판단하지 마세요. 하위 CLAUDE.md의 트리거는 read입니다.","id":"scenario-a-22","task":"3.1","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":3,"stem":"The team created `.claude/skills/release-notes/SKILL.md` with this frontmatter:\n\nname: release-notes\ndescription: Helper.\ntrigger: \"release notes, changelog, what's new\"\n\nRunning `/release-notes` directly works well, but when developers type requests like \"draft the changelog for v4.2,\" Claude rarely uses the skill. What is the most effective fix?","options":["Move the keywords into a `keywords` field and add a `version` field so that the skill loader re-indexes the skill.","Convert the skill into a subagent definition under `.claude/agents/` so that Claude delegates to it automatically.","Copy the full release-notes procedure into the root `CLAUDE.md` so that it is in context for every single request.","Rewrite `description` to state what the skill does and which requests it handles, such as drafting changelogs."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Skill의 자동 호출(auto-invocation)은 Claude가 각 skill의 `description`을 읽고 현재 요청과 맞는지 판단하는 방식으로만 이루어집니다. \"Helper.\" 같은 모호한 description은 매칭 근거가 없어 skill이 건너뛰어집니다. `trigger` 같은 필드는 존재하지 않으므로 아무 효과가 없고, 다음 사람을 오도할 뿐입니다. skill이 무엇을 하고 어떤 요청(릴리스 노트, changelog 작성)을 처리하는지 구체적으로 적으면 직접 호출과 자동 호출이 모두 신뢰성 있게 동작합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: skill 매칭 메커니즘 = description, 지어낸 필드는 무효 — Task Statement 3.2 · 출처: Section 11 (L74)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: `keywords`, `version` 역시 존재하지 않는 필드라 매칭에 영향을 주지 못합니다.\n- B: 문제는 매칭이지 실행 방식이 아닙니다. subagent 전환은 과잉 설계이며 위임 판단도 결국 description에 의존합니다.\n- C: 가끔 쓰는 다단계 절차를 상시 로드하면 모든 세션의 컨텍스트를 낭비합니다. on-demand 절차는 skill이 맞는 계층입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"직접 호출은 되는데 자동으로 안 쓰인다\" → description부터 고치세요.","id":"scenario-a-23","task":"3.2","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":3,"stem":"Claude is executing an approved eight-step plan to move `OrderRepository` from raw SQL to the ORM. At step 3, Claude discovers that a legacy batch job in `jobs/nightly/` also writes to the `orders` table. The plan assumed `OrderRepository` was the table's only writer, and steps 4–8 (schema changes, transaction boundaries, and new tests) all rely on that assumption. What should happen next?","options":["Stop, surface the discrepancy explicitly, and regenerate the plan for the remaining steps before any further changes.","Patch step 3 so it accounts for the batch job, then continue executing steps 4 through 8 exactly as approved.","Let Claude adapt the later steps on its own, since it now has the context it needs to adjust them correctly.","Revert all completed work, leave plan mode, and redo the migration with direct execution to avoid more delay."],"answer":0,"explanation":"실행 중 plan의 핵심 가정(단일 writer)이 깨졌고, 그 가정에 의존하는 downstream 단계가 4~8단계 전부입니다. 이럴 때는 re-planning이 맞습니다: 멈추고, 불일치를 명시적으로 드러내고, 남은 단계를 다시 계획한 뒤 승인받아 진행합니다. 영향이 한 단계에 국한되면 patch-and-proceed가 가능하지만, 여러 단계를 무너뜨리는 경우에는 그렇지 않습니다. 이렇게 해야 사람이 승인한 것과 실제 실행되는 코드가 일치합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 깨진 가정이 여러 downstream 단계에 영향 → patch가 아니라 re-plan — Task Statement 3.4 · 출처: Section 11 (L79)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 한 단계만 고치면 4~8단계가 여전히 틀린 가정 위에서 실행됩니다. patch는 영향이 한 단계에 국한될 때만 적절합니다.\n- C: 이것이 가장 흔한 실패인 silent improvisation으로, 승인하지 않은 변경을 리뷰하게 됩니다.\n- D: 이미 끝난 작업까지 버리고 오히려 위험한 작업에서 계획 관문을 없애는 과잉 반응입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"남은 작업 중 깨진 가정에 의존하는 부분이 얼마나 되나?\"가 re-plan vs patch의 판단 기준입니다.","id":"scenario-a-24","task":"3.4","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":1,"stem":"The team's `/review-refactor` command asks Claude to review a 60-file refactoring PR in one pass. Reviewers report that comments on the first dozen files are detailed, comments on later files are shallow, and two bugs caused by mismatched contracts between `services/quote/` and `web/src/cart/` were missed entirely. How should the review be decomposed?","options":["Review each file in a focused local pass, then run a separate integration pass that checks cross-file contracts and data flow.","Keep the single pass but add \"be thorough and check every file with equal care\" to the command's prompt before the review.","Split the files randomly into four batches, review them independently, and concatenate the four comment lists into one.","Let Claude invent its own subtasks while it browses, since fixed sequential pipelines cannot handle any code review work."],"answer":0,"explanation":"한 번에 60개 파일을 보면 주의가 분산되어 뒤쪽 파일 리뷰가 얕아지고(attention dilution), 파일 간 계약 불일치 같은 교차 이슈도 놓칩니다. 이 작업은 단계가 미리 정해진 리뷰이므로 prompt chaining 방식의 고정 분해가 적합합니다: 파일별 local pass로 각 파일의 문제를 일관된 깊이로 찾고, 별도의 cross-file integration pass로 서비스 간 계약과 데이터 흐름을 검사합니다. 두 관점을 분리하면 각 패스가 단일 책임에 집중해 누락이 줄어듭니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 대규모 multi-file 리뷰 → per-file local pass + cross-file integration pass — Task Statement 1.6 · 출처: Section 3 (L11, L12)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 구조적 한계(주의 분산)를 프롬프트 문구로만 해결하려는 시도라 효과가 없습니다.\n- C: 무작위 배치는 관련 파일을 서로 다른 배치로 갈라 놓아 교차 계약 버그를 여전히 놓치고, 통합 검토도 없습니다.\n- D: 동적·적응형 분해는 범위가 열린 조사 작업에 맞습니다. 단계가 예측 가능한 리뷰에는 고정 분해가 더 신뢰할 만합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"뒤쪽 파일 리뷰가 얕다 + 교차 버그 누락\" → 파일별 패스와 통합 패스로 나누는 것이 정답 패턴입니다.","id":"scenario-a-25","task":"1.6","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":3,"stem":"After Claude generates the new `rate-quote` module, a developer finds five problems: (1) currency rounding in `computeTotal` and (2) the order in which discounts are applied in the same function, where fixing either one changes the correct expected output of the other; (3) a typo in a log message; (4) a missing JSDoc block on an exported function; and (5) an import order that violates the lint rules. How should the developer deliver this feedback?","options":["Send all five problems in one message, since batching every issue together always beats fixing them in sequence.","Raise the two interacting problems in separate turns so each change can be verified fully in isolation.","Ask Claude to \"review the module again and improve it,\" letting it rediscover and repair all five problems.","Give the two interacting problems together in one message, then handle the three independent ones in turn."],"answer":3,"explanation":"반올림과 할인 적용 순서는 서로의 정답을 바꾸는 상호작용하는(interacting) 문제이므로, 한 메시지에 함께 제시해야 Claude가 둘을 일관되게 동시에 해결합니다. 따로 고치면 한쪽 수정이 다른 쪽의 전제를 깨뜨려 수정이 서로 충돌하거나 되돌려집니다. 반면 오타, JSDoc, import 순서는 독립적인 문제라 순차적으로 하나씩 처리하면 각 변경을 검증하기 쉽고 이미 잘된 부분을 잃지 않습니다. 이것이 iterative refinement에서 피드백을 묶을지 나눌지 판단하는 기준입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 상호작용하는 이슈는 한 메시지로 묶고, 독립 이슈는 순차적으로 — Task Statement 3.5 · 출처: Section 14 (L95)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 묶는 것이 \"항상\" 낫지는 않습니다. 독립 이슈까지 한꺼번에 주면 큰 변경이 되어 검증이 어려워집니다.\n- B: 상호작용하는 문제를 분리하면 한쪽 수정이 다른 쪽 기대값을 바꿔 서로 충돌하는 수정이 반복됩니다.\n- C: \"더 좋게 해 줘\" 같은 일반 피드백은 대규모 재작성을 낳고 구체적 문제를 확실히 고친다는 보장이 없습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"서로 영향을 주는 수정\"이라는 단서가 있으면 그 둘만 묶고 나머지는 순차 처리하세요.","id":"scenario-a-26","task":"3.5","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":3,"stem":"Atlas's root `CLAUDE.md` has grown to about 650 lines: global security rules plus long sections for React components, Terraform modules, and SQL migrations. Developers report that Claude follows the rules less consistently than before, and that a large share of each session's context is consumed before any code is read. What is the best restructuring?","options":["Rewrite the whole file with capitalized \"MUST\" and \"NEVER\" wording so that the most critical rules stand out more clearly.","Move every section into `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` on each machine so the committed project file stays short and focused.","Keep global rules in the root file and move the topic sections into `.claude/rules/` files scoped with `paths` globs.","Split the topic sections into skills marked `disable-model-invocation: true` so they load only when someone asks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"시작 시 로드되는 내용이 많을수록 작업 공간이 줄고, CLAUDE.md가 약 200줄을 넘으면 준수율(adherence)이 떨어지기 시작합니다. 전역 보안 규칙처럼 어디서나 필요한 것은 root에 남기고, React, Terraform, SQL처럼 특정 파일에만 의미 있는 규칙은 `.claude/rules/` 아래 주제별 파일로 나누어 `paths` glob으로 범위를 지정합니다. 그러면 해당 파일을 읽을 때만 규칙이 로드되어 always-on 컨텍스트가 작아지고, 규칙은 필요한 순간에 정확히 적용됩니다. 주제별 파일은 PR에서 리뷰하고 유지보수하기도 쉽습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 비대한 CLAUDE.md → 전역 규칙은 root, 주제별 규칙은 path-scoped rules로 분리 — Task Statement 3.3 · 출처: Section 10 (L67, L68)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 강조어를 늘려도 파일 크기와 컨텍스트 비용이라는 근본 원인은 그대로입니다.\n- B: 팀 표준을 user scope로 옮기면 커밋되지 않아 다른 기여자 세션에서 조용히 사라집니다.\n- D: 파일을 만질 때마다 지켜야 하는 상시 관례를 수동 호출에 의존하게 만들면 규칙이 적용되지 않는 경우가 생깁니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"CLAUDE.md가 너무 커서 준수율 하락\" → 모듈화와 path-scoped conditional loading이 정답 방향입니다.","id":"scenario-a-27","task":"3.3","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":2,"stem":"Claude tries to change `timeout: 3000` to `timeout: 5000` for the FastFreight carrier client in `services/quote/config.ts`. The Edit tool call fails because `timeout: 3000` appears three times in the file, once in each of three carrier client blocks. Only the FastFreight value should change. What is the best next step?","options":["Switch to Bash and run `sed -i 's/3000/5000/g'` on the file so every occurrence is updated in one command.","Retry Edit with an `old_string` that includes nearby unique context, such as the FastFreight client's name.","Use Grep to locate all three occurrences, then call Edit again with exactly the same `old_string` value.","Rewrite the whole file with Write from memory, since Edit can never target text that appears more than once."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Claude Code의 Edit 도구는 `old_string`이 파일 안에서 유일하게(unique) 일치할 때만 치환하며, 여러 곳에 일치하면 의도치 않은 수정을 막기 위해 실패합니다. 해결책은 `old_string`에 FastFreight 블록의 클라이언트 이름 같은 주변 문맥을 포함해 대상이 하나로 특정되게 만드는 것입니다. 이렇게 하면 원하는 한 곳만 정밀하게 바뀌고 나머지 두 클라이언트 설정은 보존됩니다. 이는 Edit을 targeted modification 도구로 올바르게 쓰는 방법입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: Edit 실패(비고유 일치) → 고유해질 때까지 주변 문맥을 `old_string`에 포함 — Task Statement 2.5 · 출처: Section 9 (L59), Section 8 (L56)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 전역 치환은 세 클라이언트 모두를 바꾸고, `3000`이 들어간 다른 값까지 망가뜨릴 수 있습니다.\n- C: 위치를 찾는 것은 유용하지만 같은 `old_string`으로 다시 호출하면 여전히 비고유라 실패합니다.\n- D: Write로 파일 전체를 다시 쓰는 대안은 Read로 현재 내용을 읽은 뒤에만 안전하며, \"기억으로\" 쓰면 다른 내용이 손상될 수 있습니다.\n\n시험 팁: Edit의 핵심 제약은 \"old_string 유일성\"입니다. 실패하면 문맥을 넓히세요.","id":"scenario-a-28","task":"2.5","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":3,"stem":"Jun and Ara are pair programming on Atlas. The project `CLAUDE.md` says \"Indent TypeScript with 2 spaces.\" Ara's sessions follow it, but Jun's sessions sometimes produce tab-indented files. Both have pulled the latest commit, and neither sees any error. What should they do first?","options":["Add \"project rules take precedence\" to the top of Jun's user file, because the closer file always wins conflicts.","Run `/memory` in both sessions to compare which memory files load, then look for a conflicting user-level rule.","Delete both developers' `~/.claude` folders and rerun `/init`, because stale cached settings cause this drift.","Move the indentation rule into `CLAUDE.local.md`, because it loads last and so overrides any user-level rule."],"answer":1,"explanation":"같은 커밋인데 사람마다 동작이 다르면, 차이는 각자의 세션에 로드된 메모리 파일에서 나올 가능성이 큽니다. 먼저 `/memory`로 양쪽 세션에 어떤 CLAUDE.md가 로드됐는지 비교해 원인을 확인하는 것이 올바른 첫 단계입니다. Jun의 user-level 파일에 \"tabs\" 같은 규칙이 있다면 project 규칙과 정면 충돌(genuine conflict)이며, CLAUDE.md 사이에는 신뢰할 수 있는 precedence가 없어 결과가 비결정적입니다. 원인을 확인한 뒤에는 충돌하는 user 규칙을 제거하거나 범위를 좁혀 모순 자체를 없애야 합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 세션 간 동작 차이 → `/memory`로 로드된 파일 확인, 충돌은 우선순위가 아니라 제거로 해결 — Task Statement 3.1 · 출처: Section 10 (L64)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: \"가까운 파일이 이긴다\"는 보장된 규칙이 아니며, 진단 없이 문구만 추가하는 것은 첫 단계가 될 수 없습니다.\n- C: 원인 확인 없이 개인 설정 전체를 지우는 파괴적 조치이며, `/init`은 starter CLAUDE.md 생성 명령입니다.\n- D: local 파일이 로드 순서상 뒤라고 해서 override가 보장되지 않고, 팀 규칙을 git-ignored 개인 파일에 두는 것도 잘못입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"왜 팀원과 다르게 동작하나?\" 진단의 첫 수는 `/memory`입니다.","id":"scenario-a-29","task":"3.1","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":3,"stem":"`.claude/commands/new-endpoint.md` contains 40 lines of API conventions copied from the root `CLAUDE.md`, followed by the steps for scaffolding a new endpoint. Last week the team changed the error envelope in `CLAUDE.md` to `{ error: { code, message } }`. Endpoints generated through `/new-endpoint` still sometimes use the old `{ code, message }` envelope. What is the best fix?","options":["Copy the updated conventions into the command file as well, and add a CI reminder telling authors to keep both in sync.","Move the command into `~/.claude/commands/` so each developer can maintain their own up-to-date copy of the rules.","Add a line to the command saying \"if a rule here conflicts with `CLAUDE.md`, prefer the rule in `CLAUDE.md`\" instead.","Remove the duplicated conventions so the command relies on `CLAUDE.md` and contains only the scaffolding steps."],"answer":3,"explanation":"CLAUDE.md는 이미 세션 전체에 상시 컨텍스트로 로드되므로, command 파일에 같은 규칙을 복제하면 두 출처가 어긋나는 drift와 유지보수 부채가 생깁니다. 지금의 불일치는 낡은 복사본과 새 규칙이 동시에 컨텍스트에 있어 생긴 정면 충돌입니다. 근본 해결책은 중복을 제거해 command가 CLAUDE.md를 확장(build on)하고, 자신만의 고유한 내용(엔드포인트 생성 절차)만 담게 하는 것입니다. 그러면 규칙은 단일 출처에서 관리되어 앞으로도 어긋나지 않습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: command는 CLAUDE.md를 반복하지 말고 그 위에 쌓아야 함 — 단일 출처 유지 — Task Statement 3.2 · 출처: Section 11 (L72)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 복제를 유지한 채 동기화를 사람 기억에 맡기므로 같은 drift가 다시 발생합니다.\n- B: 팀 워크플로를 개인 scope로 옮기면 공유가 깨지고 복사본이 사람 수만큼 늘어 drift가 더 심해집니다.\n- C: 낡은 규칙이 여전히 컨텍스트에 남아 충돌을 일으키며, 우선순위 문구가 항상 지켜진다는 보장도 없습니다.\n\n시험 팁: command 라이브러리를 망치는 두 anti-pattern = 과도하게 넓은 명령, CLAUDE.md 지시 복제.","id":"scenario-a-30","task":"3.2","scenario":"Code Generation with Claude Code","scenarioIntro":"Corvane Logistics is a freight-pricing company whose 40-person platform team builds everything in a single monorepo called Atlas. The repository contains `services/` (Node.js/TypeScript pricing and quoting APIs), `web/` (a React dashboard), `infra/` (Terraform that manages live AWS resources), `jobs/` (legacy nightly batch scripts), and `generated/` (an OpenAPI client that is regenerated on every build). Engineers use Claude Code daily for code generation, refactoring, debugging, and documentation. The team keeps a project `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root, a growing library of custom slash commands under `.claude/commands/`, and several team skills under `.claude/skills/`. Test files are colocated next to the source files they cover across all packages rather than living in a central `tests/` folder. The platform team also runs an internal MCP server, `corvane-tickets`, exposed over Streamable HTTP and protected by a per-engineer API token, so that Claude can read and update work tickets. Security policy forbids committing any credential to the repository, and every Terraform change must be reviewed by a human before it is applied. Leadership's goals for the quarter are consistent conventions across every engineer's sessions, safer large-scale refactors, and less rework caused by Claude making unstated assumptions."},{"domain":1,"stem":"A client asks for \"the economic and grid impacts of heat-pump adoption across the Nordic countries.\" The final report covers only residential adoption in Sweden, Norway, and Finland; it says nothing about commercial or district-heating installations and omits Denmark and Iceland entirely. The trace shows the coordinator created three tasks: \"residential heat-pump adoption in Sweden,\" \"...in Norway,\" and \"...in Finland.\" Each subagent completed its assigned task thoroughly, and the synthesis agent faithfully reported everything it received. What is the most likely root cause of the coverage gap?","options":["The web-research subagent built queries that were too narrow and should be instructed to broaden searches beyond its assigned subtopic.","The synthesis subagent dropped the commercial and district-heating material while compressing a large volume of subagent outputs.","The web_search tool's result limit truncated relevant sources about the other countries before they reached any of the subagents.","The coordinator decomposed the brief too narrowly, so the gaps were introduced at task assignment rather than during subagent execution."],"answer":3,"explanation":"로그상 각 서브에이전트는 배정받은 범위를 충실히 수행했고 synthesis도 받은 내용을 그대로 보고했습니다. 즉 누락은 실행 단계가 아니라 coordinator의 task decomposition 단계에서 이미 발생했습니다. 브리프의 \"economic and grid impacts\", \"across the Nordic countries\"라는 범위가 세 개의 residential 과제로 축소되면서 상업용·지역난방 설치와 덴마크·아이슬란드가 처음부터 할당되지 않았습니다. 오케스트레이터는 master plan을 가진 유일한 컴포넌트이므로, 서브에이전트 실패나 누락의 1순위 원인은 부실한 scoping입니다. 해결책은 coordinator가 분해 후 원래 브리프의 모든 차원(국가, 부문, 영향 유형)이 과제에 매핑되었는지 확인하도록 하는 것입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 서브에이전트가 \"맡은 일을 다 했는데\" 결과에 구멍이 있다면 원인은 coordinator의 분해 범위 — Task Statement 1.2 · 출처: Section 4 (L16), Section 3 (L10)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 서브에이전트에게 배정 범위를 넘어 검색하라고 하면 경계가 무너지고 중복·충돌이 생깁니다. 서브에이전트는 할당된 과제를 제대로 수행했습니다.\n- B: synthesis는 받은 것을 충실히 보고했고, 상업용 자료는 애초에 수집된 적이 없습니다.\n- C: 다른 국가에 대한 과제 자체가 생성되지 않았으므로 도구의 결과 수 제한은 원인이 될 수 없습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"각 서브에이전트는 정상 완료\"라는 단서가 보이면 실행이 아니라 분해·할당 단계를 의심하세요.","id":"scenario-a-31","task":"1.2","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":1,"stem":"The coordinator invokes the document-analysis subagent with this prompt: \"Analyze the uploaded documents and extract the claims relevant to the client's question.\" The subagent returns generic summaries of every document, flags no claims as relevant, and uses an output layout the synthesis agent cannot parse. At that point the coordinator's own context contains the client brief, the web-research findings, and the report outline. What is the most effective fix?","options":["Configure the subagent to inherit the coordinator's conversation history so it automatically sees the brief and the earlier findings.","Place the client brief in the subagent's AgentDefinition system prompt so that every invocation of the subagent shares it.","Give the subagent a callback tool for querying the coordinator whenever it decides that it is missing some piece of context.","Write the client question, the relevant prior findings, and the required output schema directly into the prompt passed at invocation."],"answer":3,"explanation":"서브에이전트는 blank context로 시작하며 coordinator의 대화 이력, 다른 에이전트의 결과, master plan을 자동으로 상속하지 않습니다. 따라서 \"the client's question\"이라고만 쓰면 서브에이전트는 그 질문이 무엇인지 알 방법이 없습니다. 올바른 context passing은 호출 시 프롬프트에 task, relevant context(브리프와 관련 선행 결과), output format, constraints를 명시적으로 담는 것입니다. 출력 스키마를 함께 지정하면 synthesis가 파싱하지 못하는 문제도 동시에 해결됩니다. 필요한 최소한의 정보만 골라 넘기는 것이 isolation의 이점(less bloat, lower cost)도 유지합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 서브에이전트는 명시적으로 받은 것만 안다 — 호출 프롬프트에 질문·관련 결과·출력 형식을 직접 포함 — Task Statement 1.3 · 출처: Section 4 (L17, L19)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 서브에이전트는 부모의 대화 이력을 상속하지 않으며, 설령 전체 이력을 넘긴다 해도 컨텍스트 비대와 누출을 일으킵니다.\n- B: 브리프는 의뢰마다 바뀌는 동적 정보입니다. 정적인 AgentDefinition 프롬프트에 넣을 수 없고 선행 결과와 출력 형식 문제도 남습니다.\n- C: 필요한 정보를 처음부터 넘기면 되는 상황에서 왕복 통신 채널을 추가하는 것은 과잉 설계이며, 서브에이전트가 무엇이 빠졌는지 알아챈다는 보장도 없습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"inherit\", \"automatically sees\"라는 표현이 있는 선택지는 서브에이전트 문제에서 거의 항상 오답입니다.","id":"scenario-a-32","task":"1.3","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":2,"stem":"The web-research subagent has two tools. `search_web` is described as \"Searches for information.\" `search_client_corpus` is described as \"Searches documents.\" When an analyst asks about figures in the client's own uploaded board minutes, the agent calls `search_web` about 60% of the time and returns public news coverage instead of the minutes. Both tools work correctly when called. What should the team do first?","options":["Rewrite both descriptions to state each tool's data source, suitable query types, example requests, and when to choose the other tool.","Add a system-prompt rule telling the agent to always try search_client_corpus first and fall back to search_web only on empty results.","Merge the two tools into one search tool with a free-text `source` parameter that the agent fills in to choose where to look.","Add a dozen few-shot examples to the system prompt that pair typical analyst questions with the correct tool for each one."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Claude는 tool description을 주된 근거로 도구를 선택합니다. \"Searches for information\"과 \"Searches documents\"는 둘 다 모호하고 서로 겹쳐, 모델이 어떤 경우에 어느 도구를 써야 하는지 구분할 정보가 없습니다. 각 도구가 어떤 데이터 소스를 다루는지, 어떤 질의에 적합한지, 예시 요청, 그리고 다른 도구와의 경계(when to use the other tool)를 설명에 명시하는 것이 근본 원인을 고치는 가장 낮은 비용의 첫 조치입니다. 도구 자체는 정상 동작하므로 문제는 오직 라우팅 정보 부족입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 도구 오선택의 1차 원인과 1차 해결책은 description — 데이터 소스·용도·경계를 명시 — Task Statement 2.1 · 출처: Section 6 (L32, L33)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 프롬프트 우회책으로, 공개 정보 질문에도 불필요하게 corpus를 먼저 검색하게 만들고 빈 결과가 아닌 \"엉뚱한 결과\"에는 대응하지 못합니다.\n- C: 경계를 없애고 자유 텍스트 파라미터에 선택을 떠넘기면 같은 모호성이 파라미터로 옮겨갈 뿐입니다.\n- D: few-shot은 보조 수단일 수 있지만 description이 빈약한 근본 원인을 그대로 둔 채 프롬프트 토큰만 늘립니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"description이 한 줄짜리\"라는 단서가 있으면 정답은 거의 항상 description 개선입니다.","id":"scenario-a-33","task":"2.1","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":5,"stem":"During a large engagement, the web-research subagent's search backend times out on 3 of its 8 queries. For each timed-out query the subagent returns `{\"status\": \"complete\", \"results\": []}`. The coordinator treats these as finished searches, and the final report states that \"no published evidence was found\" on three subtopics, which a client later disproves within minutes. What is the most effective change?","options":["Have the subagent return a structured failure with error type, the attempted query, any partial results, and possible alternatives.","Have the subagent retry each failed query without limit until it succeeds, so that empty result sets are never returned upstream.","Have the subagent raise an exception that terminates the whole research run, so that no incomplete report is ever produced.","Instruct the coordinator to treat every empty result set as a probable failure and automatically re-run the subagent for it."],"answer":0,"explanation":"이 장애의 본질은 access failure(타임아웃)가 valid empty result(정말 결과 없음)로 위장된 silent failure입니다. 서브에이전트는 실패를 구조화된 오류 컨텍스트(failure type, attempted query, partial results, alternative approaches)로 coordinator에 전파해야 합니다. 그래야 coordinator가 재시도, 대체 경로, 또는 보고서에 \"coverage gap\"으로 명시하는 결정을 내릴 수 있습니다. 복구 판단은 전체 계획을 가진 coordinator의 몫이고, 서브에이전트는 무엇이 실패했는지 정확히 보고하는 것이 역할입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: Empty result ≠ access failure — 실패는 유형·시도 내용·부분 결과를 담은 구조화 오류로 상위에 전파 — Task Statement 5.3 · 출처: Section 17 (L117, L118)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 무한 재시도는 영구 장애에서 작업을 멈추게 하고, 실패 사실을 coordinator가 알 기회를 없앱니다.\n- C: 일부 실패로 전체 워크플로를 중단하는 것은 과잉 반응이며, 이미 성공한 5개 질의의 결과까지 버립니다.\n- D: 정말 결과가 없는 정상적인 빈 결과까지 실패로 취급하게 되어 불필요한 재실행이 생깁니다. 구분은 의미를 아는 서브에이전트가 상태로 표시해야 합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"empty results\"와 \"timeout\"이 함께 나오면 정답은 둘을 구분하는 구조화된 상태/오류 필드입니다.","id":"scenario-a-34","task":"5.3","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":1,"stem":"Lumenfold handles two request types. \"Vendor due-diligence briefs\" always need the same five sections (ownership, financials, litigation, sanctions screening, ESG), in a fixed order. \"Emerging-risk investigations\" are open-ended: what to research next depends heavily on what the first searches reveal. Today both go through the same coordinator prompt, which plans subtasks dynamically. Due-diligence briefs occasionally skip the sanctions section, while investigations perform well. What is the best design?","options":["Keep dynamic planning for both request types and add a reminder listing the five mandatory sections to the coordinator prompt.","Move both request types onto one fixed five-stage chain so that investigations follow the same reliable structure as briefs.","Let the client pick at intake whether the coordinator should plan dynamically or follow a checklist for that particular request.","Run due-diligence briefs through a fixed sequential pipeline and keep adaptive decomposition for the open-ended investigations."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Task decomposition 전략은 작업의 성격에 맞춰야 합니다. 단계와 순서가 미리 정해진 실사 브리프는 fixed sequential pipeline(prompt chaining)이 적합하며, 다섯 섹션을 코드 구조로 보장하므로 sanctions 누락이 원천적으로 사라집니다. 반대로 다음 조사 대상이 중간 결과에 따라 달라지는 신흥 리스크 조사는 adaptive(dynamic) decomposition이 필요하고, 현재 이 유형은 잘 동작하고 있습니다. 두 유형을 같은 방식으로 처리하는 것이 문제의 원인이므로, 요청 유형별로 다른 분해 패턴을 쓰는 것이 최선입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 예측 가능한 고정 단계 → fixed pipeline / 결과 의존적 탐색 → adaptive decomposition — Task Statement 1.6 · 출처: Section 3 (L11, L12, L14)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 필수 섹션 보장을 프롬프트 리마인더에 맡기는 것은 확률적이며, 구조로 보장할 수 있는 곳에서 이미 실패한 방식을 반복합니다.\n- B: 고정 체인은 탐색 경로가 결과에 따라 달라지는 조사형 작업의 적응성을 없애 현재 잘 되던 유형을 망가뜨립니다.\n- C: 아키텍처 결정을 고객에게 떠넘기는 것이며, 요청 유형이 이미 명확하므로 시스템이 결정해야 합니다.\n\n시험 팁: 두 종류의 작업이 나오면 \"각각에 맞는 패턴\"을 고르는 선택지가 정답인 경우가 많습니다.","id":"scenario-a-35","task":"1.6","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":1,"stem":"Contract terms require that no report reach a client until the citation-verifier subagent has confirmed every citation in that exact draft. The coordinator's system prompt says: \"Always run citation verification and confirm it passed before calling deliver_report.\" Audits show that in about 4% of engagements, mostly very long ones, the coordinator called `deliver_report` either before verification ran or after it failed. What is the most effective fix?","options":["Move the rule to the top of the system prompt, mark it as CRITICAL, and repeat it just before the delivery step description.","Add few-shot examples showing the coordinator running verification and checking the result before each delivery call.","Add a programmatic gate that blocks deliver_report unless a passing verification record exists for that same draft ID.","Have the synthesis agent stamp a \"verified\" flag on each draft, and have deliver_report check for that flag before sending."],"answer":2,"explanation":"계약상 반드시 지켜야 하는 순서 제약은 prompt instruction이 아니라 programmatic enforcement로 보장해야 합니다. 프롬프트 지시는 아무리 강조해도 확률적으로 따르므로, 긴 세션처럼 컨텍스트가 커지는 상황에서 4% 같은 실패율이 남습니다. `deliver_report` 호출을 가로채 같은 draft ID에 대한 passing verification record가 있을 때만 허용하는 prerequisite gate(예: 코드 레벨 검사나 hook)는 실패율을 0으로 만듭니다. draft ID 단위로 묶어야 이전 버전의 통과 기록으로 수정된 초안이 나가는 것도 막을 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 결정적 준수가 필요한 워크플로 순서 = 코드 게이트, 프롬프트는 확률적 — Task Statement 1.4 · 출처: Section 4 (L20), Section 2 (L6)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 강조와 반복은 준수율을 조금 높일 수 있으나 보장은 못 하며, 특히 긴 세션에서 여전히 실패합니다.\n- B: few-shot 역시 프롬프트 기반이라 확률적이며, 규정 준수 요건을 충족시키지 못합니다.\n- D: 검증을 하지 않는 synthesis 에이전트의 자기 표시는 실제 검증 결과가 아니므로 게이트 역할을 할 수 없습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"must never\", \"contract requires\", \"audit shows X% violations\"가 보이면 프로그래밍 방식 강제를 고르세요.","id":"scenario-a-36","task":"1.4","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":4,"stem":"The document-analysis subagent's instructions already describe the required claim format in detail: verbatim quote, source ID, and locator. Outputs remain inconsistent on the hard cases. For HTML exports and slide decks with no page numbers, it sometimes invents page numbers, sometimes leaves the locator blank, and sometimes switches to paraphrase instead of quoting. Standard paginated PDFs are handled correctly. What is the most effective next step?","options":["Expand the written instructions with a longer set of rules describing the correct locator format for each document type in the corpus.","Add a few targeted examples for the ambiguous cases, such as unpaginated sources, each showing the expected output and why.","Lower the subagent's temperature so that its formatting decisions become deterministic across similar documents in the corpus.","Add a validator that rejects any extracted claim without a page number and automatically retries the extraction until one appears."],"answer":1,"explanation":"상세한 지시가 이미 있는데도 애매한 케이스에서만 출력이 흔들린다면, 추가 규칙보다 few-shot examples가 가장 효과적입니다. 페이지 번호가 없는 HTML이나 슬라이드에 대해 \"섹션 제목이나 슬라이드 번호를 locator로 쓰고, 그래도 없으면 명시적으로 null + 이유를 기록\" 같은 기대 출력을 추론과 함께 보여 주면, 모델이 판단 기준을 일반화할 수 있습니다. 예시는 이미 잘 처리되는 일반 PDF가 아니라 실패가 발생하는 경계 사례를 겨냥해 2~4개 정도로 구성하는 것이 좋습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 지시가 충분한데 모호한 케이스에서 일관성이 깨지면 → 이유를 포함한 targeted few-shot — Task Statement 4.2 · 출처: Section 14 (L89, L90)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 이미 상세한 지시가 실패하고 있는 상황에서 규칙을 더 늘리는 것은 같은 접근을 반복하는 것입니다.\n- C: temperature는 무작위성만 줄일 뿐 애매한 경우에 무엇이 올바른 판단인지 알려 주지 못합니다.\n- D: 페이지 번호가 존재하지 않는 소스에 페이지 번호를 강요하면 오히려 조작된 locator를 유도해 provenance를 훼손합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"상세한 지시가 이미 있다 + 애매한 사례에서만 불일치\"는 few-shot 문제의 전형적 신호입니다.","id":"scenario-a-37","task":"4.2","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":1,"stem":"An analyst spent two hours in an Agent SDK session in which the coordinator gathered and analyzed 60 sources for a client. Before drafting, the analyst wants to compare two report framings, one centered on implementation cost and one on regulatory exposure. Both must build on the exact same research baseline, and neither framing's drafting discussion should influence the other. What is the best approach?","options":["Resume the research session, request the cost framing first, and then request the regulatory framing later in the same session.","Start two brand-new sessions and re-run the complete research phase in each, so that each framing has its own evidence base.","Fork the research session into two branches, one per framing, so both share the baseline but diverge independently afterward.","Ask the coordinator to write a short prose recap of the research, then paste that recap into two new sessions, one per framing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Session forking(`fork_session`)은 기존 세션의 상태를 그대로 복제해 서로 독립적으로 진행되는 분기를 만드는 기능입니다. 두 프레이밍 모두 동일한 연구 기반(60개 소스의 수집·분석 결과)을 공유해야 하고, 서로의 초안 논의가 섞이면 안 된다는 요구 조건에 정확히 부합합니다. 같은 세션에서 순차적으로 진행하면 첫 번째 프레이밍의 논의가 두 번째에 영향을 주고, 처음부터 다시 조사하면 비용이 크고 기반이 달라집니다. fork는 이런 divergent exploration from a shared baseline을 위해 존재합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 공유 기반에서 서로 다른 접근을 독립적으로 비교 = fork_session — Task Statement 1.7 · 출처: Section 4 (L22), Section 18 (L124)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 같은 세션에서 연속 진행하면 첫 프레이밍의 논의가 두 번째 프레이밍의 컨텍스트에 남아 독립성이 깨집니다.\n- B: 두 시간짜리 조사를 반복하는 비용이 크고, 검색 결과가 달라져 \"동일한 기반\"이라는 요건도 충족하지 못합니다.\n- D: 짧은 산문 요약은 세부 수치·출처 정보를 잃어 \"정확히 같은 기반\"이 되지 못합니다. 손실 없이 분기하는 fork가 더 적합합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"same baseline + explore alternatives independently\"는 fork의 정의 그 자체입니다.","id":"scenario-a-38","task":"1.7","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":5,"stem":"Two subagents return conflicting figures for the share of new homes in Region R using heat pumps. A government energy agency report, published in 2023 and based on 2022 permit data, gives 31%. An industry-association survey from 2025, based on installer responses, gives 38%. The synthesis agent's draft states: \"Approximately 34.5% of new homes use heat pumps.\" What is the best fix?","options":["Instruct the synthesis agent to always prefer the most recent source whenever figures conflict, and to drop the older figure from the draft.","Have subagents report each claim with source, date, and method, and have synthesis present both figures attributed, with the conflict noted.","Instruct the synthesis agent to use only the government figure, because public agencies are the more authoritative source for such statistics.","Have the synthesis agent compute a reliability-weighted average of the two figures, based on its own assessment of each source's quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"초안의 34.5%는 어떤 출처에도 존재하지 않는 수치로, 충돌을 조용히 섞어 버린 averaging anti-pattern이며 provenance를 완전히 끊습니다. 두 수치는 측정 시점(2022 vs 2025 무렵)과 방법론(허가 데이터 vs 설치업체 설문)이 달라 둘 다 타당할 수 있습니다. 따라서 서브에이전트가 claim-source mapping(출처, 발행일, 방법론)을 구조화해 넘기고, synthesis는 두 값을 각각 귀속(attribution)해 함께 제시하고 충돌을 명시해야 합니다. 이렇게 해야 고객이 시간 차이와 방법론 차이를 보고 스스로 판단할 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 충돌하는 출처는 섞지 말고 귀속과 함께 병기하고 충돌을 주석 — 날짜·방법론 메타데이터 보존 — Task Statement 5.6 · 출처: Section 19 (L131, L132)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 최신 우선 규칙은 방법론 차이를 무시하고, 여전히 타당한 정보를 독자에게서 숨깁니다.\n- C: 권위 기반 규칙도 다른 시점의 유효한 데이터를 버리며, 충돌 사실 자체가 보고서에서 사라집니다.\n- D: 가중 평균 역시 어떤 출처에도 없는 수치를 만들어 내는 averaging이며, 모델의 주관적 판단까지 더해집니다.\n\n시험 팁: 두 출처의 중간값이 보고서에 등장하면 그것은 항상 오답의 증거이며, 정답은 \"attributed + conflict annotated\"입니다.","id":"scenario-a-39","task":"5.6","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":2,"stem":"To \"make it more capable,\" the team gave the synthesis subagent all 14 tools in the system, including `web_search`, `fetch_url`, `load_document`, and `extract_tables`. Since then, it often launches fresh research mid-draft, synthesis latency has tripled, and it sometimes picks the wrong tool. Logs show that about 85% of its tool calls are simple checks of one specific fact, such as a date or a figure, while the rest are genuine new research. What is the best design?","options":["Limit the synthesis agent to its core tools plus a scoped verify_fact tool, and route genuine new research back through the coordinator.","Keep all 14 tools and set tool_choice to \"any,\" so that the synthesis agent is forced to commit to a tool call on every turn.","Remove every tool from the synthesis agent, so that each fact check, however small, must make a round trip through the coordinator.","Keep all 14 tools and add a system-prompt instruction telling the synthesis agent to search only when it is absolutely necessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"에이전트에게 역할과 무관한 도구를 많이 주면 선택 정확도가 떨어지고 역할 밖의 행동(초안 중 새로운 조사)을 유발합니다. 원칙은 least privilege — 역할에 필요한 도구만 배정하는 것입니다. 다만 호출의 85%가 단순 사실 확인이라는 점을 고려하면, 모든 확인을 coordinator 왕복으로 보내는 것은 지연을 크게 늘립니다. 그래서 흔한 요구는 범위가 좁은 `verify_fact` 도구로 직접 처리하고, 진짜 새로운 조사는 coordinator를 통해 적절한 서브에이전트로 보내는 것이 최적의 tool distribution입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 역할별 최소 도구 + 빈번한 단순 요구에는 scoped cross-role tool, 복잡한 요구는 coordinator 경유 — Task Statement 2.3 · 출처: Section 6 (L39, L41)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: `tool_choice: \"any\"`는 매 턴 도구 호출을 강제할 뿐, 도구 과다로 인한 오선택과 역할 이탈을 오히려 악화시킵니다.\n- C: 원칙은 맞지만 85%에 달하는 단순 확인까지 모두 왕복시키면 지연이 커지는 과잉 교정입니다.\n- D: 프롬프트 지시는 도구 14개가 노출된 구조적 문제를 해결하지 못하고, \"absolutely necessary\"는 판단 기준이 모호합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"도구를 다 줬더니 이상해졌다\"는 문제는 역할별 축소가 정답이고, 빈도 높은 단순 요구에는 좁은 전용 도구를 더합니다.","id":"scenario-a-40","task":"2.3","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":1,"stem":"For a comparative brief, the coordinator must research four countries whose subtasks are completely independent of one another. The design calls for running the four web-research subagents concurrently, but traces show the coordinator issues one subagent call per turn, waits for its result, then issues the next, so wall-clock time is roughly four times longer than planned. What change most directly achieves the intended concurrency?","options":["Add a `parallel: true` setting to the web-research subagent's AgentDefinition so that the SDK schedules all of its invocations at once.","Have the first web-research subagent hand off to the next one when it finishes, so the coordinator no longer waits between countries.","Raise the coordinator's max_turns limit so that it has enough turns available to schedule the four subagents side by side.","Instruct the coordinator to emit all four subagent calls together in a single response rather than spreading them across turns."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Coordinator가 서브에이전트를 병렬로 실행하려면 하나의 응답 안에서 여러 개의 subagent(Task) 호출을 동시에 생성해야 합니다. 턴마다 하나씩 호출하고 결과를 기다리면 구조상 순차 실행이 되어 전체 시간이 합산됩니다. 네 국가의 과제는 서로 독립적이므로 fan-out에 적합하며, 결과는 coordinator가 모두 받은 뒤 fan-in(집계)하면 됩니다. 이는 오케스트레이터가 자신의 출력 방식을 바꾸는 문제이지, 서브에이전트 설정이나 턴 수 문제가 아닙니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 병렬 서브에이전트 = coordinator가 한 응답에 여러 subagent 호출을 함께 내보냄 — Task Statement 1.2 · 출처: Section 3 (L13), Section 4 (L16)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: AgentDefinition에는 그런 병렬 실행 설정이 없으며, 병렬성은 coordinator의 호출 방식에서 결정됩니다.\n- B: 서브에이전트 간 연쇄 handoff는 여전히 순차 실행이며, coordinator의 집계·감시 역할도 우회합니다.\n- C: max_turns는 루프 상한일 뿐 동시 실행 여부와 무관하며, 늘려도 순차 패턴은 그대로입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"independent subtasks + 순차 실행 로그\"는 단일 응답에 여러 호출을 내보내는 것이 정답입니다.","id":"scenario-a-41","task":"1.2","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":5,"stem":"In a three-hour session, the coordinator accumulates findings from dozens of subagent runs, and its context is compacted twice. Early in the session it recorded \"Installed capacity grew 17.3% between 2019 and 2024 (Source S12, Table 4).\" The final executive summary instead says \"Capacity grew significantly over the past several years,\" with no figure, dates, or source. Several other quantitative findings were degraded the same way. What is the most effective fix?","options":["Move the coordinator onto a model with a larger context window so that compaction is never triggered during long client engagements.","Keep figures, dates, and source IDs in a structured findings block outside the summarized history, injected into every prompt.","Instruct the coordinator to summarize more carefully during compaction, preserving every important number, date, and source.","Have each subagent return the complete raw text of its sources, so the coordinator keeps every detail available verbatim."],"answer":1,"explanation":"반복되는 요약·compaction은 구체적인 수치, 날짜, 출처를 \"significantly\" 같은 모호한 표현으로 압축해 손실시킵니다. 이를 막는 표준 패턴은 핵심 사실을 요약 대상이 되는 대화 이력과 분리된 구조화 블록(persistent fact block)에 보관하고 매 프롬프트에 주입하는 것입니다. 이 블록에 수치·기간·source ID를 함께 저장하면 compaction이 몇 번 일어나도 수치와 출처 귀속이 그대로 보존됩니다. 서브에이전트 결과를 처음부터 구조화된 형태로 받으면 이 블록을 채우기도 쉽습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: Summaries lose facts → 핵심 수치·날짜·출처는 요약 밖의 구조화된 persistent fact block에 — Task Statement 5.1 · 출처: Section 16 (L109, L110)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 더 큰 윈도우는 문제를 늦출 뿐이며, 긴 컨텍스트 중간의 정보가 덜 활용되는 문제도 남습니다.\n- C: \"더 신중히 요약하라\"는 지시는 확률적이며, 요약이 반복될수록 손실이 누적되는 구조는 그대로입니다.\n- D: 원문 전체를 넘기면 tool-output bloat로 컨텍스트가 더 빨리 차서 compaction이 오히려 잦아집니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"compaction 후 수치가 모호해짐\"이 보이면 정답은 요약 밖에 보관되는 구조화된 사실 블록입니다.","id":"scenario-a-42","task":"5.1","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":1,"stem":"A new coordinator is deployed with the Agent SDK. Four subagents (web research, document analysis, synthesis, and citation verification) are registered under the `agents` option, each with a clear description and its own tool list. In testing, the coordinator never delegates; it answers from its own knowledge and once states, \"I don't have a way to hand this task to another agent.\" The coordinator's options include `allowedTools: [\"Read\", \"Grep\", \"WebFetch\"]`. What is the most likely cause?","options":["The subagent descriptions are too generic, so the coordinator cannot recognize which registered subagent matches each part of the brief.","The subagents lack the coordinator's tools in their own lists, so the SDK quietly declines to make any of them available for use.","The coordinator's system prompt never states which types of tasks should be delegated to which of the four registered subagents.","The coordinator's allowedTools omits the subagent-spawning tool (Task/Agent), so it has no mechanism to invoke the registered subagents."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Agent SDK에서 coordinator가 서브에이전트를 호출하는 수단은 서브에이전트 생성 도구(Task, 현재 이름은 Agent tool)입니다. `agents` 옵션에 서브에이전트를 등록해도 coordinator의 `allowedTools`에 이 도구가 없으면 위임할 방법 자체가 없습니다. \"I don't have a way to hand this task to another agent\"라는 발언과 allowedTools 목록이 정확히 이 원인을 가리킵니다. 설명이나 프롬프트 개선은 위임 메커니즘이 존재한 뒤에야 의미가 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 서브에이전트 호출에는 coordinator의 allowedTools에 Task(Agent) 도구가 반드시 포함되어야 함 — Task Statement 1.3 · 출처: Section 11 (Agent SDK 보충), Section 4 (L17)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 각 서브에이전트에 명확한 description이 있다고 명시되어 있으며, 설명 문제라면 \"위임 수단이 없다\"는 발언이 나오지 않습니다.\n- B: 서브에이전트가 coordinator와 같은 도구를 가져야 할 필요는 없습니다. 오히려 역할별로 다른 도구를 주는 것이 권장됩니다.\n- C: 위임 기준을 프롬프트에 적는 것은 유용하지만, 생성 도구가 없으면 어떤 지시로도 위임할 수 없습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"서브에이전트가 전혀 호출되지 않음 + allowedTools 목록 제시\"는 Task/Agent 도구 누락을 확인하라는 신호입니다.","id":"scenario-a-43","task":"1.3","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":4,"stem":"After drafting a 30-page report, the synthesis session is asked, \"Review your report and flag any claim not supported by its cited source.\" It flags two minor issues. A later client audit finds nine claims whose cited passages do not support them; most are confident restatements of the draft's own interpretations. What is the most effective improvement to the review step?","options":["Have the same synthesis session review its report two more times, each pass using a stricter checklist of unsupported-claim patterns.","Use a separate reviewer instance without the drafting context that checks each claim against the excerpt of its cited source.","Enable extended thinking for the synthesis session so it reasons more thoroughly while it reviews the report it has just written.","Have the synthesis agent rate its confidence in each claim, and automatically remove every claim that scores below 0.7 from the report."],"answer":1,"explanation":"같은 세션이 자신의 결과물을 검토하면 작성 시의 추론 컨텍스트를 그대로 가지고 있기 때문에 자신의 해석을 다시 정당화하는 경향이 있어 오류를 놓칩니다. 효과적인 방법은 독립된 reviewer instance가 작성 맥락 없이 각 claim을 인용된 출처 원문 발췌와 1:1로 대조하는 것입니다. 이는 multi-instance review의 핵심 이점이며, claim 단위로 검토하면 30페이지 분량에서도 주의가 희석되지 않습니다. 감사에서 발견된 오류가 대부분 \"초안 자체의 해석을 확신 있게 재진술한 것\"이라는 점이 self-review의 한계를 보여 줍니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 자기 검토는 생성 맥락에 묶임 → 컨텍스트가 분리된 독립 인스턴스가 claim-by-source로 검증 — Task Statement 4.6 · 출처: Section 15 (L103)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 같은 세션으로 반복 검토해도 같은 추론 편향이 그대로 유지되어 동일한 오류를 계속 놓칩니다.\n- C: extended thinking은 추론량을 늘리지만, 자신의 초안 맥락에 묶인 근본적 한계는 해결하지 못합니다.\n- D: 모델의 자기 보고 신뢰도는 보정되지 않았으며, 이번 오류들은 \"확신 있는\" 진술이라 오히려 높은 점수를 받을 가능성이 큽니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"self-review가 놓쳤다\"는 문제는 독립 인스턴스(fresh context) 리뷰가 정답입니다.","id":"scenario-a-44","task":"4.6","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":1,"stem":"An analyst resumes yesterday's Agent SDK session by its session ID to continue an engagement. Overnight, the client replaced 14 of the 20 uploaded documents with revised versions that restate many key figures, and several cited web pages were updated. In the resumed session, the coordinator confidently quotes figures from the old document versions, relying on tool results already stored in its history. What is the best approach?","options":["Start a new session seeded with a structured summary of findings still valid, and mark the revised documents for fresh analysis.","Continue in the resumed session as-is, because the stored tool results remain the authoritative record of what the research found.","Fork the resumed session, so the stale branch is preserved while the new branch continues from the same stored tool results.","Continue in the resumed session and add an instruction telling the coordinator to double-check any figure it feels unsure about."],"answer":0,"explanation":"세션 resume은 대화 이력과 그 안의 tool result를 그대로 복원하므로, 외부 세계가 바뀌면 이력 속 결과는 stale 상태가 됩니다. 이번에는 20개 중 14개 문서가 교체되어 이력의 대부분이 낡은 데이터이므로, 낡은 결과가 가득한 세션을 이어 가기보다 유효한 결과만 구조화 요약으로 담아 새 세션을 시작하는 것이 더 신뢰할 수 있습니다. 변경된 문서를 명시적으로 재분석 대상으로 표시하면 무엇을 다시 확인해야 하는지도 분명해집니다. 반대로 변경이 소수 파일에 국한된다면 resume 후 해당 파일만 알려 주고 재분석하는 방식이 적합합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 이전 tool result 대부분이 stale이면 resume보다 구조화 요약을 넣은 새 세션 — Task Statement 1.7 · 출처: Section 4 (L22), Section 18 (L124)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 저장된 tool result는 과거 시점의 스냅샷일 뿐이며, 바뀐 문서를 반영하지 못해 지금과 같은 잘못된 인용이 계속됩니다.\n- C: fork는 같은 낡은 이력을 복제하므로 stale 데이터 문제를 그대로 가져갑니다. fork는 대안 탐색용입니다.\n- D: 모델은 이력의 결과를 확신하고 있어 \"불확실하다\"고 느끼지 않으므로, 이 지시는 거의 작동하지 않습니다.\n\n시험 팁: resume vs fresh start는 \"이전 tool result가 아직 유효한가\"로 판단합니다. 대부분 낡았다면 새 세션 + 구조화 요약입니다.","id":"scenario-a-45","task":"1.7","scenario":"Multi-Agent Research System","scenarioIntro":"Lumenfold Advisory, a public-policy consultancy, runs an internal research engine built on the Claude Agent SDK that produces cited briefing reports for government and enterprise clients. A coordinator agent receives each client brief, decomposes it into research tasks, and delegates them to specialized subagents through the subagent-spawning tool (Task, now also called the Agent tool). The web-research subagent has `web_search` and `fetch_url`; the document-analysis subagent has `load_document` and `extract_tables` for the client's uploaded PDFs, spreadsheets, and HTML exports; the synthesis subagent drafts the report; and a citation-verifier subagent checks that every cited passage actually exists in its source. Each subagent starts with its own isolated context, so the coordinator is responsible for everything a subagent needs to know. Reports run 15–40 pages, and contracts require that every factual claim be traceable to a specific source, publication date, and locator. Engagements frequently span several working sessions, and analysts sometimes resume or branch earlier sessions. Because clients use these reports in regulatory filings, a fabricated citation or a silently missing topic is far more costly than a slower turnaround. The engineering team's goals are complete topic coverage, reliable error handling across agents, and faithful, well-attributed synthesis."},{"domain":4,"stem":"In the `record_shipment` tool schema, `port_of_discharge` is defined as a required `string`. About 9% of documents are inland transfers that state no discharge port at all. Audits show that for these documents Claude often fills the field with a real, plausible port taken from the shipper's address block, and these values pass the UN/LOCODE lookup. Which schema change BEST addresses this while keeping the downstream API working?","options":["Remove `port_of_discharge` from the `required` list so Claude can omit the key whenever the document does not state a discharge port.","Keep the field a required string and tell Claude in its description to return `\"UNKNOWN\"` whenever the document gives no discharge port.","Keep the schema unchanged and add a business rule that discards any port value matching a city that appears anywhere within the shipper's address block.","Keep the key required but make its type `[\"string\", \"null\"]`, and describe it as null when no discharge port is stated, never inferred from addresses."],"answer":3,"explanation":"데이터가 항상 존재하지 않는 필드를 required string으로 두면 모델은 무언가를 채워야 한다는 압박을 받아 그럴듯한 hallucinated value를 만들어 냅니다. 이 시나리오에서는 하류 customs-filing API가 키 누락은 거부하지만 `null`은 허용하므로, 키는 required로 유지하면서 타입을 nullable(`[\"string\",\"null\"]`)로 바꾸는 것이 두 제약을 동시에 만족합니다. 여기에 field description으로 \"문서에 명시되지 않으면 null, 주소에서 추론하지 말 것\"이라는 boundary case를 적어 주면 부재가 정상적인 예상 결과라는 신호가 모델에 전달됩니다. 이렇게 하면 \"추출된 값\"과 \"근거 없음\"의 구분이 하류까지 보존됩니다. UN/LOCODE 검사는 실제 존재하는 항구라면 통과시키므로, 환각의 원인을 고치는 것은 스키마 설계입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 기반 데이터가 매번 값을 보장할 때만 non-null required — 부재 가능 필드는 null 허용 + 경계 설명 — Task Statement 4.3 · 출처: Section 15 (L98)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 환각 압박은 줄지만 키가 사라지므로 키 누락을 거부하는 하류 API가 레코드를 반려합니다. 하류가 생략을 처리할 수 있는 경우라면 맞는 선택일 수 있습니다.\n- B: sentinel 기본값은 형태는 균일하지만 \"추출 값\"과 \"찾지 못함\"의 구분이 흐려지고, `\"UNKNOWN\"`이 실제 문자열로 하류에 흘러갈 위험이 있습니다.\n- C: 증상 일부만 거르는 사후 규칙입니다. 다른 출처(예: 운송사 주소)에서 추론한 항구는 그대로 통과하며 환각의 원인인 required 압박은 남습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"하류가 키 누락은 거부, null은 허용\" 같은 단서가 있으면 omit이 아니라 nullable required를 고르세요.","id":"scenario-a-46","task":"4.3","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":4,"stem":"DocStream switched its summary endpoint to structured outputs (`output_config.format` with a JSON schema). Most responses parse cleanly, but commercial invoices with more than ~250 line items intermittently fail JSON parsing with an unterminated array. An engineer argues that structured outputs \"is not actually guaranteeing the schema.\" What should the team do?","options":["Revert to prompting for JSON and add a repair step that closes any open brackets and arrays before the parser runs on the response.","Read `stop_reason` before parsing; on `max_tokens`, retry with a higher limit or split the line items into page-range requests.","Add `maxItems: 250` to the `line_items` array so that constrained decoding can never emit a list longer than the token budget allows.","Lower the temperature to 0 for invoice requests so the model produces shorter, more deterministic line-item descriptions every time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Structured outputs의 보장은 constrained decoding으로 생성 중에 이루어지지만, 문서화된 guarantee gap 두 가지가 있습니다. 바로 safety refusal과 max_tokens cutoff입니다. 줄 수가 많은 송장에서만 배열이 닫히지 않은 채 끝난다는 것은 출력이 토큰 한도에서 잘렸다는 신호입니다. 따라서 payload를 믿기 전에 `stop_reason`을 먼저 확인하고, `max_tokens`이면 한도를 올려 재시도하거나 요청을 쪼개는 것이 올바른 대응입니다. 이 실패는 스키마 보장이 깨진 버그가 아니라 예상된 동작입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: stop_reason을 먼저 읽고 parse — max_tokens 잘림은 스키마 위반이 아니라 guarantee gap — Task Statement 4.3 · 출처: Section 15 (L97, L99)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 생성 시점 보장을 버리고 retry/repair 발판을 되살리는 퇴보입니다. 잘린 내용은 괄호를 닫아도 복구되지 않습니다.\n- C: `maxItems`는 grammar로 강제되는 부분집합 밖의 키워드입니다(`minItems`는 0 또는 1만). 또한 항목을 잘라내면 데이터가 손실됩니다.\n- D: temperature는 분산을 줄일 뿐 출력 길이 한도 문제를 해결하지 못합니다. 다른 근본 원인을 고치는 선택지입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"가끔 JSON이 안 닫힌다\" + \"큰 입력\" = max_tokens. 정답은 언제나 stop_reason 확인부터입니다.","id":"scenario-a-47","task":"4.3","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":4,"stem":"When a record fails the business-rule layer, DocStream re-sends the original extraction prompt with one extra user turn: \"Your previous output was invalid. Please try again carefully.\" Logs show that 70% of retries fail the same check, and some retries fix the failing field but break fields that had passed before. Which change to the retry step is MOST effective?","options":["Raise the retry budget from three to eight attempts, and raise the temperature slightly on each attempt so later retries explore different outputs.","Send the specific failed checks with expected values, re-include the relevant source text, and ask Claude to correct only the failing fields.","Replace the retry with a reviewer model call that re-reads the entire document and regenerates the full record from scratch each time.","Add a sentence to the system prompt stressing that every business rule must be satisfied on the first attempt, with the rules listed in full."],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"다시 시도하라\"는 막연한 피드백은 원래 프롬프트보다 정보가 없어 같은 실패를 재현합니다. 효과적인 re-prompt는 세 원칙을 따릅니다. 첫째, 구체적인 검증 오류(어떤 검사가 실패했고 기대값이 무엇인지)를 넣습니다. 둘째, 관련 원문을 다시 포함해 이전 출력을 기억으로 고치는 대신 증거에서 재추출하게 합니다. 셋째, 실패한 필드만 수정하도록 범위를 좁혀, 전체 재생성이 이전에 맞던 필드를 깨뜨리는 문제를 막습니다. 로그에 나타난 두 증상(같은 실패 반복, 통과 필드 파손)을 정확히 겨냥하는 것은 B뿐입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: retry 프롬프트 = 구체적 오류 + 원문 재포함 + 실패 필드만 수정 — Task Statement 4.4 · 출처: Section 15 (L101, L102)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 정보가 없는 재시도를 늘리는 것은 비용만 늘리고 semantic drift 위험을 키웁니다. temperature bump는 피드백이 구체적인 상태에서 막힌 패턴을 깰 때 보조 수단입니다.\n- C: 전체 재생성은 오히려 \"통과 필드 파손\" 증상을 악화시키며, 무엇이 틀렸는지 알려 주지 않아 과설계입니다.\n- D: 프롬프트 강조는 첫 시도의 품질을 약간 바꿀 수 있지만 재시도 루프에 실패 정보를 전달하지 못합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"Please try again\"이 보이면 구체적 오류 피드백이 빠진 것입니다.","id":"scenario-a-48","task":"4.4","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":4,"stem":"For about 3% of commercial invoices, the line-item sum differs from the stated invoice total by exactly the freight charge, and all three retries fail the same check. After the third failure, the pipeline currently writes the record with `invoice_total: 0` and a `status: \"ok\"` flag so that the downstream batch does not stall. What is the BEST design change?","options":["Remove the line-item total check for invoices that list a freight charge, because the check produces failures that retries cannot resolve.","Increase the retry budget to ten attempts with a temperature bump on each attempt until the line-item sum finally matches the total.","Keep writing the zero total but add a nightly report listing these records so that analysts can correct them later in the downstream system.","Route budget-exhausted records to review with a structured error and logged attempts, and treat the repeated failure as a prompt/schema defect."],"answer":3,"explanation":"재시도 예산이 소진되었을 때 빈 값이나 기본값을 조용히 반환하는 것(silence)이 가장 위험한 실패 모드입니다. `invoice_total: 0`과 `status: \"ok\"`는 하류에 그럴듯하지만 틀린 데이터를 정상처럼 흘려보냅니다. 올바른 escalation path는 사람 검토 큐로 보내면서 실패한 검사, 시도한 값, 시도 횟수를 담은 structured error를 남기고 모든 시도를 로깅하는 것입니다. 또한 여러 시도에서 같은 semantic failure가 반복된다는 것은 무작위 불운이 아니라 설계 피드백입니다. 여기서는 freight charge를 line item에 포함할지 별도 필드로 둘지가 스키마·프롬프트에 정의되지 않았다는 신호입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 예산 소진 → 명시적 escalation(structured error/review), 반복 semantic failure = 설계 문제 — Task Statement 4.4 · 출처: Section 15 (L102)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 검사를 없애면 실제 불일치까지 통과시켜 문제를 숨깁니다. 고칠 대상은 freight charge의 정의이지 검증층이 아닙니다.\n- B: 같은 semantic failure는 프롬프트를 바꾸지 않는 한 재시도로 해결되지 않으며, 긴 재시도는 의미가 멀어지는 semantic drift를 부릅니다.\n- C: 틀린 데이터가 이미 하류에 정상 상태로 들어간 뒤의 사후 보고입니다. 고위험 필드는 하류 전파 전에 막아야 합니다.\n\n시험 팁: retry 소진 후 \"safe default + ok\" 처리는 오답 패턴, structured error + review 큐가 정답 패턴입니다.","id":"scenario-a-49","task":"4.4","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":4,"stem":"To cut costs, the CFO proposes moving all DocStream traffic to the Message Batches API: the urgent clearance lane, the 400,000-document archive backfill, and the reconciliation agent's discrepancy runs, which call `lookup_hs_code` and `fetch_exchange_rate` and act on the results. Which plan is BEST?","options":["Batch only the archive backfill, keyed by document ID; keep the urgent lane and the reconciliation agent on synchronous calls.","Batch all three workloads, and submit the urgent lane in small batches every few minutes because most batches finish within an hour.","Batch the backfill and the reconciliation agent, since batch requests support tools, and keep only the urgent clearance lane synchronous.","Keep everything synchronous, because batch processing uses a cheaper model tier that would reduce extraction accuracy on scanned documents."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Message Batches API는 같은 모델·같은 품질로 비용을 50% 줄이는 대신 시간을 거래합니다. 처리 창의 상한은 24시간이며 그 안에서 지연 보장이 없으므로, 2분 SLA가 걸린 urgent lane에는 맞지 않습니다. 배치 요청은 도구 정의와 tool call 반환을 지원하지만, 요청 중간에 도구를 실행하고 결과를 되먹이는 왕복(round trip)은 불가능한 single-turn입니다. 따라서 도구 결과에 따라 다음 행동을 정하는 reconciliation agent의 agentic loop는 동기 경로가 필요합니다. 3주의 여유가 있고 아무것도 기다리지 않는 backfill만 배치에 적합하며, 결과는 문서 ID를 custom_id로 붙여 매칭해야 합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 판단 질문 \"이것이 도는 동안 막혀 있는 것이 있는가?\" + 배치는 single-turn — Task Statement 4.5 · 출처: Section 15 (L106)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: \"보통 1시간\"은 약속이 아니라 관찰일 뿐입니다. 24시간 상한은 SLA 업무에서 예약된 장애입니다.\n- C: \"배치가 도구를 지원한다\"는 절반만 맞습니다. 도구 결과를 받아 다음 결정을 내리는 다중 턴 루프는 배치로 돌릴 수 없습니다.\n- D: 배치는 더 싼 모델이 아니라 같은 모델의 비동기 처리입니다. 잘못된 전제에 기반한 오답입니다.\n\n시험 팁: Batch = 50% 할인, 24h 상한, 지연 보장 없음, single-turn, custom_id 매칭. 이 다섯 가지를 함께 기억하세요.","id":"scenario-a-50","task":"4.5","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":4,"stem":"The extraction schema includes `contains_dangerous_goods: boolean`, described as \"true if the shipment may be hazardous.\" Reviewers report that 40% of flagged shipments are false positives, mostly product descriptions that merely mention \"lithium battery compatible\" or \"flammable-look finish.\" Each flag blocks a shipment for manual DG review. What is the MOST effective fix?","options":["Add \"only flag shipments that are truly dangerous, and be conservative when uncertain\" to the system prompt and the field description.","Define true as a UN number, hazard class, or DG declaration in the document, and state that product or marketing wording alone does not qualify.","Add a second-pass reviewer call that re-reads every document flagged as dangerous and votes on whether the flag should be kept or removed.","Ask Claude for a 0–1 hazard score instead of a boolean and only block shipments whose score is above 0.7 until a calibrated cutoff is available."],"answer":1,"explanation":"\"may be hazardous\" 같은 모호한 기준은 판단을 모델에게 떠넘기고, 모델은 위험을 연상시키는 단어만으로도 플래그를 세웁니다. False positive를 줄이는 가장 직접적인 방법은 무엇이 해당하는지에 대한 explicit criteria를 주는 것입니다. 여기서는 UN 번호, 위험물 등급, DG declaration 같은 관찰 가능한 증거를 기준으로 삼습니다. 동시에 무엇이 해당하지 않는지(제품 설명, 마케팅 문구)를 명시해 경계를 그어야 합니다. 이렇게 하면 precision이 오르고, 차단 플래그의 신뢰도가 회복되어 검토 부담도 줄어듭니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 막연한 \"신중하게/정말 위험할 때\"가 아니라 구체적 포함·제외 기준을 명시 — Task Statement 4.1 · 출처: Section 13 (L83, L84)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: \"conservative\", \"truly dangerous\"는 여전히 정의되지 않은 기준입니다. 무엇이 해당하는지를 알려 주지 않으므로 precision이 안정적으로 오르지 않습니다.\n- C: 기준이 모호한 상태에서 리뷰 패스를 붙이는 것은 비용만 늘리는 과설계입니다. 리뷰는 명확한 프롬프트의 대체물이 아닙니다.\n- D: 보정되지 않은 self-reported 점수에 임의 cutoff를 거는 방식이며, 기준이 모호하다는 근본 원인을 그대로 둡니다.\n\n시험 팁: false positive 문제의 1순위 해법은 \"explicit criteria + 무엇이 해당하지 않는지\"입니다.","id":"scenario-a-51","task":"4.1","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":4,"stem":"The B/L extraction prompt contains three few-shot examples, all taken from one large carrier whose template places the shipper box top-left and the notify party beneath the consignee. On B/Ls from other carriers, Claude increasingly swaps `shipper` and `notify_party`, and on B/Ls that say \"NOTIFY: SAME AS CONSIGNEE\" it copies the consignee's name and address into `notify_party`. What should the team do FIRST?","options":["Add seven more examples from the same carrier so that the model sees the shipper and notify-party fields placed correctly many more times.","Keep the examples and add an instruction telling Claude not to rely on the layout of the examples when reading other carriers' documents.","Replace them with diverse carrier layouts, including a \"SAME AS CONSIGNEE\" case, and place the most representative example last.","Enable extended thinking for B/L requests so that Claude reasons step by step about which party box is which before it calls the tool."],"answer":2,"explanation":"세 예시가 모두 한 운송사 템플릿에서 왔기 때문에 모델은 \"필드의 의미\"가 아니라 그 레이아웃의 위치 패턴을 학습했습니다. 이것이 example contamination과 다양성 부족의 전형적인 증상입니다. 해법은 같은 작업 안에서 레이아웃·운송사·형식을 다양화하고, \"SAME AS CONSIGNEE\" 같은 edge case를 최소 하나 포함하는 것입니다. 그 예시에서는 notify party를 어떻게 기록할지 정답 출력을 보여 줍니다. 또한 모델은 과제에 가까운 뒤쪽 예시에 더 큰 가중치를 두므로, 가장 대표적인 예시를 마지막에 둡니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 다양한 예시 3개 > 같은 영역의 많은 예시, 나쁜 예시는 교체(지시로 땜질 금지) — Task Statement 4.2 · 출처: Section 14 (L90)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 같은 좁은 영역에서 예시를 늘리면 좁은 패턴이 더 강화됩니다. 목표는 양이 아니라 커버리지의 폭입니다.\n- B: 나쁜 예시를 추가 지시로 땜질하는 것은 잘못된 방향입니다. 예시의 신호가 지시보다 강하게 작동합니다.\n- D: 추론을 늘려도 편향된 예시가 주는 신호는 그대로입니다. 비용만 늘리고 원인을 고치지 않습니다.\n\n시험 팁: 예시와 다른 입력에서 품질이 떨어지면 \"다양성 부족\", 해법은 예시 교체입니다.","id":"scenario-a-52","task":"4.2","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":4,"stem":"DocStream's schema has one field, `shipment_date`, described as \"the shipment date\" and declared with `format: \"date\"`. Values are now always valid ISO dates, yet audits find a mix of B/L issue dates, shipped-on-board dates, and estimated departure dates, and \"03/04/26\" is read inconsistently as March or April. Customs requires the shipped-on-board date. What is the BEST fix?","options":["Keep the single field and add a post-processing step that runs each value through a date-parsing library configured to normalize all values to ISO 8601.","Describe it as the shipped-on-board date, ranked above issue date and ETD, ambiguous numerals resolved by origin-country convention, null if absent.","Add five few-shot examples of correctly extracted dates, all in ISO format, so that Claude learns to output the field in one consistent format.","Tighten the field with a strict regex `pattern` for YYYY-MM-DD and require Claude to return a separate `date_confidence` score next to the value."],"answer":1,"explanation":"`format: \"date\"`는 형식(shape)을 보장할 뿐 어떤 날짜를 고를지(judgment)는 보장하지 않습니다. 문제의 본질은 description이 \"the shipment date\"처럼 이름만 반복해, 후보가 여럿일 때 모델이 스키마가 내렸어야 할 판단을 떠안는다는 점입니다. 효과적인 field description은 이 문서 유형에서 필드가 뜻하는 바, 우선순위(priority), 모호한 표기의 해석 규칙 같은 boundary case, 그리고 부재 시 처리를 명시합니다. B는 이 네 요소를 모두 갖춰 의미 오류와 dd/mm 혼동을 함께 줄입니다. 스키마는 컨테이너를 보장할 뿐 필드를 똑똑하게 만들지 않는다는 점이 핵심입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 형식 보장 ≠ 값 선택 정확도 — description에 의미·우선순위·경계·결측 규칙을 명시 — Task Statement 4.1 · 출처: Section 15 (L98), Section 13 (L83)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 이미 ISO 형식인 값을 다시 정규화할 뿐이며, 잘못된 종류의 날짜를 골랐다는 의미 오류와 월/일 모호성은 그대로 남습니다.\n- C: 형식 일관성은 이미 확보된 상태라 잘못된 문제를 겨냥합니다. 어떤 날짜가 우선인지에 대한 기준은 여전히 없습니다.\n- D: regex도 형식 제약일 뿐이고, 보정되지 않은 confidence는 어떤 날짜를 골라야 하는지 알려 주지 못합니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"값은 유효한데 의미가 틀리다\"는 description 정밀도 문제입니다. 형식 제약을 더하는 선택지는 함정입니다.","id":"scenario-a-53","task":"4.1","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":2,"stem":"The reconciliation agent has two MCP tools. `lookup_hs_code` is described as \"Looks up HS codes for products,\" and `search_tariff_schedule` is described as \"Searches tariff and HS code information.\" Traces show the agent calling `search_tariff_schedule` with a product description (which returns irrelevant duty tables) and calling `lookup_hs_code` with a 10-digit code to get duty rates. What is the MOST effective fix?","options":["Add a third routing tool, `choose_tariff_tool`, that receives the agent's intent and returns the name of the tool that should be called next.","Set `tool_choice` to force `lookup_hs_code` on every turn so that the agent always classifies the product before it searches the tariff schedule.","Rewrite both descriptions to state purpose, expected input format, output, and when NOT to use each tool, pointing to the other tool.","Add a system-prompt line asking the agent to think carefully about which tariff-related tool fits the situation before each call."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Claude는 도구를 주로 description을 보고 선택하므로, 두 설명이 모두 \"HS code\"를 언급하며 경계가 겹치면 잘못된 라우팅이 생깁니다. 해법은 각 도구가 무엇을 하는지, 어떤 입력 형식(제품 설명 vs 10자리 코드)을 받는지, 무엇을 반환하는지를 쓰는 것입니다. 무엇보다 언제 쓰지 말아야 하는지와 대신 쓸 도구를 명시해 clean separation을 만들어야 합니다. 이렇게 하면 \"제품 설명 → lookup_hs_code → 코드 → search_tariff_schedule → 관세율\"이라는 흐름이 설명 자체에서 드러납니다. 라우팅 문제를 도구 추가나 강제로 덮는 것보다 경계를 다시 쓰는 것이 근본 해결입니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 겹치는 도구는 경계를 다시 쓰거나 합친다 — 라우팅 문제를 도구 추가로 고치지 않는다 — Task Statement 2.1 · 출처: Section 6 (L33, L40)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 라우팅 실패를 고치려고 도구를 더하면 선택지가 늘어 오히려 선택 오류 표면이 커집니다(L40 \"Don't add a tool to fix routing\").\n- B: 매 턴 강제하면 이미 코드를 알고 있을 때도 불필요한 호출이 생기고, `search_tariff_schedule`의 오용은 그대로 남습니다.\n- D: 무엇이 다른지 알려 주지 않는 \"신중하게\"는 정보가 없습니다. 근본 원인인 모호한 설명이 그대로 남습니다.\n\n시험 팁: 도구 오선택 문제의 1순위 답은 \"description에 경계와 when-not-to-use 명시\"입니다.","id":"scenario-a-54","task":"2.1","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":2,"stem":"For a Sunday invoice date, the MCP tool `fetch_exchange_rate` returns `{\"rate\": null}` as a normal (non-error) result because the central bank publishes no rate on weekends. The agent treats null as 0 and files a customs value of $0.00. Company policy is to use the most recent prior business-day rate. How should the tool's response be redesigned?","options":["Return a successful result with `rate: 0` and a `note` field explaining that weekend dates have no published rate so the agent can read it.","Throw an unhandled exception inside the MCP server so the call fails loudly and the agent loop stops before any customs value is filed.","Return `is_error: true` with a stable code like RATE_NOT_PUBLISHED, the date tried, non-retryable status, and a \"use prior business day\" hint.","Have the tool retry the same request with exponential backoff until the central bank publishes a rate for the requested weekend date."],"answer":2,"explanation":"실패를 성공 상태로 반환하면서 내용 깊숙이 묻는 것은 대표적인 실수로, 에이전트는 이를 정상 결과로 보고 계속 진행합니다. `tool_result`는 `tool_use_id`, `content`, `is_error` 세 필드만 가지므로, 실패는 `is_error: true`로 표시합니다. 그리고 `content` 안에 안정적인 error code, 실패를 일으킨 입력값(context), 재시도 가능 여부, suggested action을 담습니다. 이 오류는 일시적 장애가 아니라 같은 입력으로는 다시 시도해도 해결되지 않는 유형이므로, \"직전 영업일 환율 사용\"이라는 다음 행동 힌트가 에이전트의 회복을 이끕니다. 이렇게 하면 null이 0으로 바뀌는 조용한 오류가 구조적으로 사라집니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 오류는 is_error + code·context·retryable·suggested action으로 구조화 — 성공으로 위장 금지 — Task Statement 2.2 · 출처: Section 6 (L37)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 여전히 성공으로 위장하며 0이라는 그럴듯한 값을 넘깁니다. 에이전트가 note를 읽는다는 보장이 없어 같은 사고가 반복됩니다.\n- B: 처리되지 않은 예외는 회복 정보 없이 루프를 끊습니다. 에이전트가 재계획할 수 있도록 오류를 observation으로 돌려줘야 합니다.\n- D: 영업일이 아니어서 생긴 오류는 transient가 아니므로 기다려도 해결되지 않습니다. backoff는 rate limit 같은 일시적 오류에 맞는 정책입니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"정상 응답에 null/빈 값\" 시나리오의 정답은 is_error + 구조화된 오류 내용입니다.","id":"scenario-a-55","task":"2.2","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":2,"stem":"The single-turn router call has three extraction tools: `record_bill_of_lading`, `record_commercial_invoice`, and `record_customs_declaration`. With `tool_choice: auto`, about 2% of responses are prose (\"This looks like a packing list...\") that the pipeline cannot route. Packing lists and other unsupported types do occur in the intake stream. Which configuration is BEST?","options":["Add a `flag_unsupported_document` tool and set `tool_choice: {\"type\": \"any\"}` so that every response is a call to exactly one of the four tools.","Set `tool_choice: {\"type\": \"tool\", \"name\": \"record_commercial_invoice\"}` because invoices are the most common document type in the intake stream.","Keep `tool_choice: auto` and add a system-prompt rule telling Claude to always call one of the three tools and never answer in prose.","Set `tool_choice: {\"type\": \"any\"}` with the existing three tools so that Claude must pick whichever extraction tool fits the document best."],"answer":0,"explanation":"이 호출은 반드시 행동해야 하지만 유효한 행동이 여러 개인 단계이므로 `tool_choice: any`가 맞습니다. 모델이 도구 중 하나를 반드시 호출하되 어느 것인지는 스스로 고르는 dispatcher 패턴입니다. 그러나 지원하지 않는 문서 유형이 실제로 들어오므로, 세 도구만으로 강제하면 packing list도 셋 중 하나로 잘못 밀어 넣게 됩니다. 그래서 강제 선택지 안에 정당한 탈출구인 `flag_unsupported_document`를 함께 두어야 합니다. 단일 턴 라우터이므로 `any`로 인한 루프 종료 문제도 생기지 않습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 여러 유효 핸들러 중 반드시 하나 → any, 단 강제할 때는 모든 입력에 맞는 선택지가 있어야 한다 — Task Statement 2.3 · 출처: Section 6 (L41)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: `tool` 지정은 항상 같은 고정 단계에 쓰는 설정입니다. B/L과 신고서까지 송장 도구로 보내 대량 오분류를 만듭니다.\n- C: 프롬프트 지시는 빈도를 줄일 뿐 보장하지 않습니다. 프롬프트만으로 고치는 해법이며, unsupported 문서의 처리도 정의되지 않습니다.\n- D: 산문 응답은 사라지지만 packing list가 세 도구 중 하나로 강제 오분류되어 조용한 오류가 됩니다. 가장 매력적인 함정입니다.\n\n시험 팁: 강제(any/tool)를 고를 때는 \"모든 입력에 맞는 선택지가 있는가?\"를 먼저 확인하세요.","id":"scenario-a-56","task":"2.3","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":1,"stem":"The reconciliation agent's loop is implemented as shown below. In production, about 30% of runs end after the first turn with no tools executed, even though the task required several lookups. Traces show those first responses begin with \"Let me check the HS code first.\" What is the root cause and fix?\n\nwhile True:\n    resp = client.messages.create(model=M, tools=TOOLS, messages=msgs, max_tokens=2048)\n    msgs.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": resp.content})\n    if resp.content[0].type == \"text\":\n        break\n    msgs.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": run_tools(resp.content)})","options":["The model is reasoning in text instead of acting; set `tool_choice: {\"type\": \"any\"}` on every turn so that each response must start with a tool call.","The `max_tokens` value is too small for a reasoning preamble plus a tool call; raise it to 8192 so that responses are no longer cut off.","Text can precede a `tool_use` block in one response; loop on `stop_reason`, continuing on `tool_use` and ending on `end_turn`, with a turn cap.","The system prompt allows narration; add an instruction that Claude must never write explanatory text before calling a tool in this agent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Claude는 한 응답 안에서 텍스트 블록(\"먼저 확인해 보겠습니다\") 다음에 `tool_use` 블록을 함께 낼 수 있습니다. 따라서 `content[0].type == \"text\"`로 종료를 판단하면 도구 호출이 포함된 응답에서도 루프가 너무 일찍 끝납니다. 올바른 agentic loop는 `stop_reason`으로 제어합니다. `tool_use`이면 모든 도구를 실행해 `tool_result`를 돌려주고 계속하며, `end_turn`이면 종료합니다. 무한 실행을 막는 turn cap은 런타임에서 강제하고, `max_tokens` 같은 다른 종료 사유도 따로 처리합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: 루프 종료는 stop_reason으로 판단 — 첫 content 블록이나 응답 문구로 판단하지 않는다 — Task Statement 1.1 · 출처: Section 2 (L4, L6)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 매 턴 `any`로 강제하면 모델이 끝낼 방법이 없어져 무한 루프 위험이 생깁니다. 종료 판단의 버그도 그대로 남습니다.\n- B: 응답이 잘린 것이 아니라 정상 응답을 잘못 해석한 것입니다. 잘림이었다면 `stop_reason: max_tokens`로 드러났을 것입니다.\n- D: 서두 텍스트는 정상적인 동작이며 금지할 이유가 없습니다. 프롬프트 지시는 확률적이어서 루프 버그를 고치지 못합니다.\n\n시험 팁: 루프 제어 문제에서는 \"stop_reason\"이 들어간 선택지를 먼저 검토하세요.","id":"scenario-a-57","task":"1.1","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":1,"stem":"Harborline's rule is that `submit_customs_entry` may be called only after a record has passed all validation layers, and entries above $50,000 also need a reviewer's approval. The rule is in the reconciliation agent's system prompt in bold capitals. In one quarter there were three incidents in which the agent submitted a high-value entry without approval after long discrepancy-resolution sessions. What should the team do?","options":["Enforce it in the tool's handler: block calls unless the record is validated and, above $50,000, carries a valid approval ID; return a structured error.","Repeat the rule at the end of the system prompt and in each tool description so it stays salient during long sessions with many tool results.","Add a reviewer model call that reads the agent's full transcript after each run and opens an incident ticket whenever it finds an unapproved filing.","Move the rule to the first user message, which receives more attention than the system prompt, and add an example of the agent asking for approval."],"answer":0,"explanation":"시스템 프롬프트의 규칙은 규칙이 아니라 요청이며, 모델의 준수는 확률적입니다. 긴 세션에서 사고가 났다는 것은 context drift로 초기 지시의 salience가 떨어진 전형적인 사례입니다. 신고 제출처럼 되돌릴 수 없고 규제 벌금이 걸린 고위험 경로에서는, 도구 실행 직전에 programmatic enforcement를 두어야 합니다. 즉 검증 상태와 승인 ID를 코드로 확인하는 pre-execution gate를 둡니다. 차단 시 구조화된 오류를 돌려주면 에이전트는 승인 요청이라는 올바른 handoff로 전환할 수 있습니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: \"Prompts guide behavior. Code enforces constraints.\" — 비가역·고위험 행동은 실행 전 코드 게이트 — Task Statement 1.4 · 출처: Section 5 (L28, L29)\n\n오답 분석\n- B: 반복 배치는 위반 빈도를 줄일 수 있지만 구조적으로 막지 못합니다. 고위험 경로에서는 준수율이 아니라 차단 여부가 중요합니다.\n- C: 사후 탐지는 이미 제출된 신고를 되돌리지 못합니다. 실행 후 감시는 차단(gate)이 아닙니다.\n- D: 위치를 옮겨도 여전히 프롬프트 기반 가드레일입니다. 근본적으로 확률적이라는 문제가 그대로 남습니다.\n\n시험 팁: \"프롬프트에 강하게 썼는데도 가끔 위반\" = 코드 강제(gate/hook)가 정답입니다.","id":"scenario-a-58","task":"1.4","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":1,"stem":"When retries are exhausted, DocStream hands the document to the review queue with the message \"Extraction failed — needs human review\" and the PDF attached. Reviewers spend about 11 minutes per item re-reading multi-page documents, and they sometimes \"fix\" fields that were already correct. What handoff design BEST improves this?","options":["Attach the full model conversation, including all prompts, retries, and raw outputs, so that reviewers can reconstruct everything the pipeline did.","Send only the document ID and a severity label, and let reviewers pull whatever context they need from the extraction logs on demand.","Send a structured payload: validated fields marked accepted, failing fields with attempted values, the failed checks, and source page references.","Have Claude write a free-text paragraph summarizing what went wrong with the extraction and attach it to the PDF for the reviewer to read."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Handoff는 시스템이 가장 많이 깨지는 지점이며, 받는 쪽은 보내는 쪽이 아는 것을 자동으로 알지 못합니다. 좋은 handoff는 필요한 것만, 자유 텍스트가 아니라 구조화된 schema로 넘깁니다. 이 시나리오에서는 이미 검증을 통과한 필드(손대지 말 것), 실패한 필드와 시도한 값, 실패한 검사, 원문 근거 위치가 필요합니다. 그러면 검토자는 문서 전체를 다시 읽지 않고 문제 필드만 확인할 수 있습니다. 또한 통과 필드를 accepted로 표시하면 맞는 값을 잘못 \"고치는\" 문제도 줄어듭니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: handoff = 필요한 것만, 구조화된 형태로, 이미 확정된 것과 남은 것을 명시 — Task Statement 1.4 · 출처: Section 3 (L10)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 전체 기록을 넘기면 노이즈가 늘어 검토자가 무관한 정보에 시간을 씁니다. \"필요한 것만 전달\" 원칙을 어깁니다.\n- B: 정보가 너무 적어 검토자가 다시 맥락을 재구성해야 합니다. 현재의 문제를 다른 형태로 반복할 뿐입니다.\n- D: 자유 텍스트 요약은 받는 쪽이 해석해야 하고, 어떤 필드가 확정되었는지를 기계적으로 표시하지 못합니다.\n\n시험 팁: handoff 문제에서는 \"구조화 + 필요한 것만 + 확정/미확정 구분\"이 들어간 선택지가 정답입니다.","id":"scenario-a-59","task":"1.4","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."},{"domain":5,"stem":"DocStream asks Claude to return a `confidence` value (0–1) next to each extracted field, and any field at or above 0.85 is auto-approved. A quarterly audit shows that `gross_weight_kg` values reported at about 0.9 are correct only 62% of the time, while `consignee_name` values at about 0.6 are correct 93% of the time. The team plans a model upgrade next month. What should it do?","options":["Add an instruction asking Claude to lower its confidence on weight fields, and raise the global auto-approve threshold to 0.95 for every field type.","Switch to per-record routing so that any record with a field below 0.85 goes to review in full, which removes the need to trust any field scores.","Calibrate per field type on a labeled, held-out set, set thresholds from measured accuracy, and re-run it on the same set after the upgrade.","Feed the misjudged audit records back into the prompt as few-shot examples, then reuse those same records to confirm the scores have improved."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Claude가 내는 confidence는 내부 확률이 아니라 요청에 따라 생성한 verbalized self-report입니다. 따라서 라벨이 있는 데이터로 calibration하기 전에는 라우팅 근거가 될 수 없습니다. 감사 결과는 무게 필드가 overconfident(0.9인데 62%)하고 수하인 이름이 underconfident하다는 것을 보여 줍니다. 이 경우 필드 유형별로 측정한 정확도에 맞춰 threshold를 따로 정해야 합니다. 측정에는 운영 분포를 반영하고 필드별 정답 라벨이 있는 held-out validation set을 쓰며, 모델 업그레이드나 프롬프트 변경 때마다 같은 세트로 재측정합니다. Overconfidence는 오류를 조용히 자동 승인시키므로 특히 위험합니다.\n\n핵심 개념 / 풀이 포인트: threshold는 모델의 자기 평가가 아니라 측정된 정확도에서 정한다 — 필드 유형별·반복적 calibration — Task Statement 5.5 · 출처: Section 19 (L126, L127)\n\n오답 분석\n- A: 점수를 낮추라는 지시는 여전히 보정되지 않은 self-report입니다. 전역 0.95는 이미 정확한 이름 필드까지 검토로 보내 인력을 낭비합니다.\n- B: per-record routing은 감사 단순성이 최우선일 때 맞을 수 있지만, 여전히 점수를 기준으로 라우팅하므로 과신 문제를 해결하지 못하고 검토 부담만 늘립니다.\n- D: 평가 데이터를 프롬프트 조정에 쓰면 held-out 원칙이 깨져 측정이 오염되고, 같은 데이터로 확인하면 개선이 과대평가됩니다.\n\n시험 팁: confidence 문제의 정답 키워드는 \"labeled held-out set, per-field calibration, recalibrate after changes\"입니다.","id":"scenario-a-60","task":"5.5","scenario":"Structured Data Extraction","scenarioIntro":"Harborline Logistics, a mid-sized freight forwarder, is building DocStream, a Claude-based pipeline that turns unstructured shipping documents into JSON records for its customs-filing platform. Inputs arrive as scanned PDFs and emails: bills of lading (B/L) from dozens of ocean carriers, commercial invoices, packing lists, and customs declarations, often with inconsistent layouts and OCR noise. A single-turn router call first identifies the document type; an extraction call then returns the fields through a `record_shipment` extraction tool defined with `strict: true`. Every record passes a Pydantic schema check and a business-rule layer (UN/LOCODE port lookup, HS-code format, line-item totals versus the stated invoice total) before it reaches downstream systems. The downstream customs-filing API rejects any payload with a missing key but accepts explicit `null` values, and a filing error can cost Harborline a regulatory penalty. A separate reconciliation agent, built as a manual agentic loop over the Messages API, uses MCP tools (`lookup_hs_code`, `search_tariff_schedule`, `fetch_exchange_rate`, `submit_customs_entry`) to resolve discrepancies and file entries. Two workloads coexist: an urgent clearance lane with a two-minute SLA, and a backfill of roughly 400,000 archived documents that must be re-extracted before a data-migration deadline three weeks away. A six-person review team handles low-confidence fields and failed records, and leadership wants to cut both review load and filing errors without slowing the urgent lane."}]};
